       v.skills, null, 'draft', null, null, 'civic', v.discovery_category
  from (values
    ('237b2be1-b651-5f68-9af3-f26076bb823b'::uuid, -- drawdown-deploy-alternative-insulation-materials
     'Compare insulation labels at a hardware store',
     'Visit a hardware store or its website and compare the labels and product sheets for a few kinds of insulation, such as cellulose, mineral wool, fiberglass and foam board. Note what each is made of and anything the maker says about recycled content, then turn your notes into a simple comparison chart. Post a photo of your chart.',
     'research', 'explore', 2, 100, 'review', array['research','data-analysis']::text[]),
    ('c44d0a0d-1c7f-5396-a071-80149e36c664'::uuid, -- drawdown-deploy-alternative-refrigerants
     'Find out which refrigerant your fridge uses',
     'Look for the rating label on your fridge or freezer, often inside the door or on an inner wall, which names the refrigerant it uses. Look up that refrigerant from an official or manufacturer source and write a sentence or two on what you learned. Post a photo of the label next to your note.',
     'education', 'explore', 1, 100, 'review', array['research','observation']::text[]),
    ('169089fe-4e2c-54b5-a91f-11fcde81d44d'::uuid, -- drawdown-improve-refrigerant-management
     'Share how to safely get rid of an old fridge',
     'Find out how your city, county or utility handles old fridges, freezers and air conditioners, including any pickup or drop-off service that removes the refrigerant properly. Turn the official steps into a short, friendly post or flyer for your building or neighborhood group, with links to the official pages. Post a link or photo of what you shared.',
     'education', 'create', 1, 100, 'review', array['research','writing']::text[]),
    ('7bf1aab9-7278-547d-810b-df442bb1eb04'::uuid, -- drawdown-deploy-building-automation-systems
     'Ask a public building how it controls its energy use',
     'Pick a public building you use, such as a library, school or community center, and send a short, polite question in your own words to its facilities office or the agency that runs it: does the building use automatic controls to schedule heating, cooling and lights, and who looks after them? Use the official contact form, email or a public comment period. Post your question and any reply, with names and contact details removed.',
     'advocacy', 'explore', 2, 100, 'review', array['research','writing']::text[]),
    ('72c015b4-1c69-50d5-adee-2264d5fd2a53'::uuid, -- drawdown-improve-district-heating-buildings
     'Find out if your town has shared heating pipes',
     'District heating means one central plant pipes heat to many buildings. Use public sources such as your city, university, hospital or utility websites to find out whether there is a district heating network near you, or where the nearest one is. Make a short explainer with a simple map and the sources you used, and post it.',
     'research', 'explore', 2, 100, 'review', array['research','mapping']::text[]),
    ('bcf5b9c7-0423-5586-8fba-06b57be0ff19'::uuid, -- drawdown-use-heat-pumps
     'Interview someone who heats with a heat pump',
     'Find a friend, relative or neighbor who already heats their home with a heat pump and ask a few simple questions: how it handles cold and hot days, what surprised them, and what they wish they had known. Get their permission before recording or quoting them, and leave out their address and other personal details. Post a short written or audio summary so neighbors weighing their own heating choices can hear from someone nearby.',
     'research', 'explore', 1, 100, 'review', array['interviewing','writing']::text[]),
    ('02f26a02-9e16-50ff-aa3a-ff108aa9756c'::uuid, -- drawdown-use-smart-programmable-thermostats
     'Help a neighbor set up their thermostat schedule',
     'If a family member or neighbor has a programmable or smart thermostat but has never set a schedule and would like help, sit down with them and read the manual together. Set times that keep the home comfortable when people are in and ease off when they are out or asleep, with the resident deciding every setting and doing any app sign-in themselves. Post a short note on what you set up together.',
     'mutual_aid', 'help', 1, 100, 'review', array['mutual_aid','teaching']::text[]),
    ('8d7a5b07-2074-56b3-8355-47f79877d568'::uuid, -- drawdown-improve-windows-glass
     'Map the drafty windows in your home',
     'On a cool or windy day, move slowly around each window you can reach from the floor and hold a strip of tissue paper near the edges; if it flutters, you have found a draft. Mark each drafty spot on a simple sketch of your home, and if you rent, you can share the list politely with your landlord or building manager. Post a photo of your sketch.',
     'research', 'explore', 1, 100, 'review', array['observation']::text[]),
    ('0cab1dcb-56e2-501d-87e4-bee9130bf456'::uuid, -- drawdown-deploy-agrivoltaics
     'Ask farmers at a market about solar on farmland',
     'Visit a farmers market and, when stalls are quiet, ask a few farmers what they think about putting solar panels on farmland, including setups where crops grow or animals graze under the panels. If no market is open near you, ask a farm or two the same question through their public contact pages. Take notes, and only record or photograph people who say yes. Post a short summary of what you heard, without names unless people agreed to be named.',
     'research', 'explore', 2, 100, 'review', array['interviewing','writing']::text[]),
    ('14a40713-7381-5a28-8506-03b4df42f043'::uuid, -- drawdown-deploy-distributed-solar-pv
     'Find solar options for renters in your area',
     'Many people who rent or live in apartments can''t put panels on their own roof. Look up official information from your state, regional or national energy office, or your utility, about community solar or other programs that let renters use solar power, and write a plain-language summary with links. Share it with a renters'' group, building or neighborhood group and post a link or photo.',
     'research', 'explore', 2, 100, 'review', array['research','writing','outreach']::text[]),
    ('ba11cd9a-9260-548e-b5ef-93ff0f0445db'::uuid, -- drawdown-deploy-led-lighting
     'Take a lighting inventory of your home',
     'Walk through your home and, for each lamp or light fixture you can see clearly from the floor, note whether it holds an LED, compact fluorescent, halogen or old-style bulb, using the packaging or the printing on the bulb where you can. Make a simple tally and share it with your household so you know where switching could help when bulbs burn out. Post a photo of your tally.',
     'research', 'explore', 1, 100, 'review', array['observation','data-analysis']::text[]),
    ('82ce9fb9-9081-5523-a130-c37f3dc6900a'::uuid, -- drawdown-deploy-offshore-wind-turbines
     'Write a short song about wind power at sea',
     'Write and record a short song, rap or spoken-word piece about wind turbines out at sea sending power to homes on shore, and about the people who build and look after them. A phone recording is fine; give it a title and credit everyone who helped. Post the recording and the lyrics.',
     'music', 'create', 1, 100, 'review', array['songwriting','music']::text[]),
    ('400c34d6-e2d4-5977-84a6-21373c17f230'::uuid, -- drawdown-deploy-onshore-wind-turbines
     'Comment on a wind project in a public process',
     'Look through official sources, such as your state or regional energy siting board, county planning office or national permitting portal, for a wind project that is open for public comment. Read the summary, then write a short, respectful comment in your own words about what matters to your community, and submit it, or save it as a draft for a project whose comment period opens soon. Post a link or screenshot of your comment with personal details removed.',
     'advocacy', 'create', 3, 150, 'review', array['policy-analysis','writing']::text[]),
    ('9890ab86-5e07-5dfc-ab69-40874c388b01'::uuid, -- drawdown-deploy-utility-scale-solar-pv
     'Find the nearest large solar farm on a public map',
     'Use a free public map of power plants from your national energy agency or a similar official source to find the large solar farms closest to you. Make a short post with a screenshot, each site''s name and owner if listed, and one thing you learned about it. If there''s a public hearing coming up about a new solar project near you, include the date and how to take part.',
     'research', 'explore', 2, 100, 'review', array['research','mapping']::text[]),
    ('feec02fd-a269-5c00-94ac-c16737ad7546'::uuid, -- drawdown-improve-cement-production
     'Ask your city if it buys lower-carbon concrete',
     'Concrete for sidewalks, schools and roads is often bought by local governments. Send a short, polite question in your own words to your city or county''s public works or purchasing office, or ask during a public comment period, about whether its rules allow or encourage lower-carbon concrete. Post your question and any reply, with names and contact details hidden.',
     'advocacy', 'explore', 2, 100, 'review', array['policy-analysis','writing']::text[]),
    ('940ee6f3-0ff8-528c-bc73-30f4a3a03d29'::uuid, -- drawdown-increase-centralized-composting
     'Map the food scrap drop-off spots near you',
     'Find out whether your city or local services collect food scraps for composting, through curbside pickup, drop-off points or farmers markets. Make a simple map or list with locations, hours and what''s accepted, and share it with neighbors. If nothing exists, send a polite question in your own words to your council member instead and post that, with names and contact details hidden.',
     'community', 'help', 1, 100, 'review', array['research','mapping']::text[]),
    ('39c075dc-ce16-5321-b1d7-5b75b916a3cb'::uuid, -- drawdown-deploy-industrial-green-hydrogen
     'Look up hydrogen projects planned in your region',
     'Search official sources, such as your energy department, regional development agency or permitting portals, for hydrogen projects planned near you, and note whether they would make hydrogen with renewable electricity. Write a short, neutral summary with links, including any public meetings or comment periods. Post it.',
     'research', 'explore', 2, 100, 'review', array['research','policy-analysis']::text[]),
    ('5ce73068-1f93-55dd-a858-c36c2ebeb612'::uuid, -- drawdown-improve-landfill-management
     'Find out which landfill takes your trash',
     'Use your local waste agency''s website to learn where your household trash ends up, then look for public information on whether that landfill collects the gas it gives off. Write a short summary with links and share it with neighbors. If the information isn''t public, send a polite question to the agency and post that.',
     'research', 'explore', 2, 100, 'review', array['research','writing']::text[]),
    ('34dcd492-e437-500b-8818-fd9dfaa3fbbc'::uuid, -- drawdown-increase-recycling
     'Make a recycling sign for your building',
     'Get your area''s official recycling rules and turn them into a clear, one-page sign showing what goes in the recycling for metals, paper and cardboard, plastics and glass, with pictures if you can. Ask your building manager, school or community center for permission to post it. Post a photo of the sign in place.',
     'community', 'create', 1, 100, 'review', array['design','community']::text[]),
    ('69a6d95a-447b-5cdc-9d60-064b8dc01d6f'::uuid, -- drawdown-increase-carpooling
     'Organize a carpool for one regular trip',
     'Pick one regular trip that several people you know make, such as getting to work, school, practice or worship, and set up a simple sign-up sheet or group chat so people can share rides. Agree on times, public meeting spots and how you''ll handle changes; if the riders are children, set it up only among their parents or guardians. Post a photo of your sign-up sheet or schedule with names and contact details hidden.',
     'community', 'help', 2, 100, 'review', array['organizing','community']::text[]),
    ('6b7e9acb-e697-56e8-beb4-417333d2c5db'::uuid, -- drawdown-mobilize-electric-bicycles
     'Make a guide to e-bike rules where you live',
     'Find the official rules for electric bicycles in your city, state or country, such as where they can be ridden, age limits and helmet rules, plus any official e-bike share or lending program. Make a one-page guide with links to the official sources and share it with a neighborhood or school group. Post a photo or link of your guide.',
     'education', 'create', 2, 100, 'review', array['research','writing']::text[]),
    ('febe45f0-f1d6-57ef-a5f4-73ed7e4985c4'::uuid, -- drawdown-mobilize-electric-cars
     'Map the public car chargers in your neighborhood',
     'Use a free public charging station map, such as one run by your government, to find electric car chargers near you. Mark them on a simple map and note which neighborhoods, apartment areas or main streets have few or none. Post your map with the source.',
     'research', 'explore', 1, 100, 'review', array['mapping','research']::text[]),
    ('0b3adca4-63f1-50aa-a3d8-1fdd8426d787'::uuid, -- drawdown-mobilize-electric-seated-scooters-motorcycles
     'Ask a local scooter shop about electric models',
     'Visit a motorcycle or scooter shop during business hours and ask the staff which electric models people ask about, what riders like, and what holds them back. Take notes, with a photo only if they agree, then write a short summary. Post it.',
     'business', 'explore', 2, 100, 'review', array['interviewing','writing']::text[]),
    ('e2aa8ccd-9bc3-5941-8e81-3d3cd8cbb57c'::uuid, -- drawdown-mobilize-hybrid-cars
     'Compare your car''s fuel economy with a hybrid',
     'Look up the official fuel economy rating for the car your household uses, or one you see often, on your government''s fuel economy website, and compare it with a hybrid version or a similar hybrid model. Make a simple side-by-side chart. Post a photo of your chart and the source.',
     'research', 'explore', 1, 100, 'review', array['research','data-analysis']::text[]),
    ('7fd3053d-e1af-5477-a656-1a38e6569588'::uuid, -- drawdown-improve-nonmotorized-transportation
     'Do a walk audit of a route to a school or park',
     'Walk a short route that kids or neighbors use to reach a school, park or library, and note anything that makes walking or biking hard, such as missing sidewalks, broken curb ramps or long waits at crossings. Report the issues through your city''s official service request or feedback channel. Post your notes and a screenshot of your report.',
     'advocacy', 'explore', 1, 100, 'review', array['observation','writing']::text[]),
    ('a87e5275-c212-51bf-8650-22af893a7fd0'::uuid, -- drawdown-enhance-public-transit
     'Rate the bus stops near you and report back',
     'Visit a few bus or tram stops near you and note what each one has, such as a shelter, a bench, lighting, a posted schedule, and a smooth path for wheelchairs and strollers. Send a short, polite summary to your transit agency through its official feedback channel. Post your notes and the message you sent.',
     'advocacy', 'explore', 1, 100, 'review', array['observation','writing']::text[]),
    ('8b493fa5-e6c6-5b83-8ac7-83741aa8882d'::uuid, -- drawdown-reduce-crop-residue-burning
     'Explain what farmers can do with leftover stalks',
     'After harvest, fields are left with stalks, leaves and husks that are sometimes burned. Using reliable sources, find out other things farmers do with these leftovers, such as leaving them as mulch or using them for animal bedding, and make a short explainer post, poster or video. Post it with your sources.',
     'education', 'create', 2, 100, 'review', array['research','teaching']::text[]),
    ('e86c2226-e09f-59d4-90e6-3a8106cf4c2c'::uuid, -- drawdown-improve-diets
     'Share a plant-rich family recipe with neighbors',
     'Cook a favorite dish built mostly on beans, grains, vegetables or other plant foods, maybe one from your family or culture, and write it up as a simple recipe card. Share it with neighbors or at a potluck, listing the main ingredients so people with allergies can check. Post a photo of the dish and the card.',
     'community', 'create', 1, 100, 'review', array['cooking','writing']::text[]),
    ('ed9a7f1a-93f5-5ed7-852e-e99ed689ff36'::uuid, -- drawdown-reduce-food-loss-waste
     'Track a week of food waste at home',
     'For one week, keep a simple log of food your household throws away, what it was and why, such as forgotten leftovers or buying too much. At the end of the week, pick one easy change to try and share it with friends or neighbors. Post a photo of your log and your chosen change.',
     'research', 'explore', 1, 100, 'review', array['observation','data-analysis']::text[]),
    ('6fae6f0d-c160-57ef-9977-3bed661fb77a'::uuid, -- drawdown-improve-nutrient-management
     'Share your area''s lawn fertilizer rules',
     'Farmers aren''t the only ones who use fertilizer; lawns and gardens get it too. Look up official rules or guidance in your area about when and where lawn fertilizer may be used, such as near streams or in certain seasons, and make a short, friendly post or flyer with the official link. Post a photo or link of what you shared.',
     'education', 'create', 1, 100, 'review', array['research','writing']::text[]),
    ('1321d44c-b8ca-5f2e-975d-a7c1487d5cd0'::uuid, -- drawdown-improve-rice-production
     'Explain how rice can be grown with less methane',
     'Most rice grows in flooded fields, and the standing water lets methane form in the soil. Read reliable sources about growing methods that let fields dry out between floodings, and make a short explainer, comic or video in plain words. Post it with your sources.',
     'education', 'create', 2, 100, 'review', array['research','teaching']::text[]),
    ('31490c0d-4a7a-5e86-a3a7-9904e1b872ad'::uuid, -- drawdown-improve-annual-cropping
     'Make a cover crop guide for local gardeners',
     'Cover crops are plants grown between harvests to protect bare soil. Use your local agricultural advisory service, a university garden program or another reliable source to find which cover crops suit gardens in your area and when to sow them, then make a one-page guide for a community garden or gardening group. Post a photo or link of your guide.',
     'education', 'create', 2, 100, 'review', array['research','gardening','writing']::text[]),
    ('5a898376-c3f7-57b3-9029-be155f809f2f'::uuid, -- drawdown-protect-coastal-wetlands
     'Map the coastal wetlands nearest to you',
     'Use public maps from a coastal, wildlife or parks agency to find the salt marshes, mangroves or seagrass beds nearest to where you live, and which of them are protected. Make a simple map with a note on who manages each place. Post your map with sources.',
     'research', 'explore', 2, 100, 'review', array['research','mapping']::text[]),
    ('e459b18c-7352-5f7c-b93c-d5cb383f850c'::uuid, -- drawdown-protect-forests
     'Find out who looks after the forest nearest you',
     'Use public maps and agency websites to find the forest nearest you and learn who manages it and whether it is protected, for example as a park, a reserve, or community or Indigenous land. Check whether any plan for it is open for public comment. Write a short summary with links and post it.',
     'research', 'explore', 2, 100, 'review', array['research','mapping']::text[]),
    ('b2a88b65-1e5b-5da4-9af7-011ca8f7874f'::uuid, -- drawdown-protect-grasslands-savannas
     'Find the protected grasslands in your region',
     'Use a public protected-areas map or your parks agency''s website to find grasslands, prairies or savannas in your region and which of them are protected. Make a simple map and add a note on one place you could visit on a public trail. Post your map with sources.',
     'research', 'explore', 2, 100, 'review', array['research','mapping']::text[]),
    ('f0533986-f7c6-53bd-82b4-c311e9875cb3'::uuid, -- drawdown-protect-peatlands
     'Check garden store soil bags for peat',
     'Many potting mixes contain peat dug from peatlands. Visit a garden store or browse its website, read the labels on a few bags of potting soil and compost, and note which contain peat and which say peat-free. Post a photo of your notes or a short list.',
     'research', 'explore', 1, 100, 'review', array['observation','research']::text[]),
    ('960f0604-0a15-5012-aef8-a70418b535e3'::uuid, -- drawdown-protect-seaweed-ecosystems
     'Make a short video about kelp forests',
     'Learn about wild kelp and seaweed forests from reliable sources, such as an aquarium or a marine agency, then make a short video, slideshow or comic explaining where they grow and what lives in them. Post it with your sources.',
     'education', 'create', 1, 100, 'review', array['video','research']::text[]),
    ('216568f0-243f-5cac-91b9-4b4ae8b571ed'::uuid, -- drawdown-restore-forests
     'Join an organized tree-planting or care day',
     'Find a tree-planting, watering or forest care day run by a park agency, conservation group or other organizer that welcomes public volunteers, and join it. If none is happening this week, help spread the word about the next one. Post a photo of your work or a link to where you shared the event.',
     'community', 'help', 2, 100, 'review', array['community','outdoors']::text[]),
    ('5b79bc68-40a5-5a3a-835f-23ab6b83e99e'::uuid, -- drawdown-restore-peatlands
     'Find a bog or fen restoration project to follow',
     'Peatlands such as bogs and fens can be restored by rewetting them and bringing back the plants that form peat. Find a restoration project in your country through a conservation group, park agency or university, and write a short summary of what it is doing and how people can follow or volunteer with it. Post it with links.',
     'research', 'explore', 2, 100, 'review', array['research','writing']::text[]),
    ('1c2eaace-0753-5afa-b538-dc8989ed529e'::uuid, -- drawdown-deploy-silvopasture
     'Draw a pasture where trees and animals share land',
     'Silvopasture means growing trees on land where animals graze. Look at photos and descriptions from reliable sources, then draw or paint a scene that shows how the trees, grass and animals fit together, with simple labels. Post a photo of your artwork with your sources.',
     'creative', 'create', 1, 100, 'review', array['drawing','research']::text[]),
    ('60df48e0-d185-5852-99ae-7bf2a245e853'::uuid, -- drawdown-use-biochar
     'Ask a garden center what it knows about biochar',
     'Biochar is a charcoal-like material made from plant and farm leftovers that can be added to soil. Ask staff at a garden center, nursery or community garden whether they sell or use it and what people ask about it, then write a short summary. Post your summary.',
     'research', 'explore', 1, 100, 'review', array['interviewing','writing']::text[]),
    ('3a9da222-581a-51ec-b5ae-a2599c35f46d'::uuid, -- drawdown-boost-appliance-equipment-efficiency
     'Teach friends how to read an appliance energy label',
     'Find the official energy label used for appliances where you live, then look at a few real labels in a store or online. Make a short post, poster or video that explains in plain words what each part of the label means and where to find more help. Post a link to it or a photo of it.',
     'education', 'create', 1, 100, 'review', array['teaching','design']::text[]),
    ('ff5325cd-8f20-5ccf-9949-089b806a1d54'::uuid, -- drawdown-improve-building-envelopes
     'Share where to find free or low-cost weatherization help',
     'Look up official programs in your area that help households seal drafts and add insulation at low or no cost, such as government weatherization assistance or utility efficiency programs. Write a short, plain-language list with each program''s name, who it is for and a link to its official page, then share it online or, with permission, on a library or community notice board where renters and older neighbors will see it. Post a photo or link showing where you shared it.',
     'mutual_aid', 'help', 2, 100, 'review', array['research','writing','outreach']::text[]),
    ('1b0ab594-ac54-5909-a768-a35e518a1449'::uuid, -- drawdown-deploy-green-roofs
     'Find out how your city treats green roofs',
     'Search your city''s official website, building rules or climate plan for anything about green roofs, meaning roofs covered with growing plants. Write a short summary of what you found, and if you found nothing, send a polite question to a council member or the planning office asking whether the city has considered them. Post your summary with source links, or a screenshot of your question.',
     'advocacy', 'explore', 2, 100, 'review', array['research','policy-analysis','writing']::text[]),
    ('f7eeae72-b28f-5183-a392-f527edaf73ec'::uuid, -- drawdown-use-low-flow-fixtures
     'Measure how much water your shower uses',
     'Hold a bucket or large pot of known size under your shower head or kitchen tap, turn the cold water on fully, and time how long it takes to fill. Work out roughly how much water flows each minute, then check your water utility''s website for free or low-cost water-saving kits for households. Post a photo of your notes and a link to anything useful you found.',
     'research', 'explore', 1, 100, 'review', array['observation','data-analysis']::text[]),
    ('9d1fdc5d-7617-5408-9269-8937cde77c7a'::uuid, -- drawdown-deploy-cool-roofs
     'Map light and dark roofs in your neighborhood',
     'Open the satellite view of a free online map and pick a few blocks of a neighborhood you know; it doesn''t have to be your own. Mark which roofs look light-colored and which look dark, then make a simple map or tally that shows the pattern, noting public places like schools, libraries or senior centers where staying cool matters most. Post a screenshot or photo of your marked-up map or tally.',
     'research', 'explore', 1, 100, 'review', array['mapping','observation']::text[]),
    ('a6793da7-d182-5fa1-bf42-59bbc9796347'::uuid, -- drawdown-increase-decentralized-composting
     'Volunteer at a community garden compost day',
     'Find a community garden, school garden or compost site near you that welcomes volunteers, and join a scheduled work session to help turn or sift compost. If nothing is scheduled this week, visit during open hours and ask how they compost and how neighbors can drop off scraps. Post a photo of your work or a short note on what you learned.',
     'community', 'help', 1, 100, 'review', array['community','gardening']::text[]),
    ('56b4c743-10a0-5148-ae60-323c3e0d1564'::uuid, -- drawdown-improve-fishing-vessel-efficiency
     'Ask a fish seller how their fish are caught',
     'Visit a fish counter, market stall or fishmonger at a quiet time and ask where their fish come from, what kind of boats caught them and how far the boats travel. Take notes, and take a photo of the display only with permission. Post a short summary of what you learned.',
     'research', 'explore', 1, 100, 'review', array['interviewing','writing']::text[]),
    ('cdc236e3-e4bd-5323-bcd4-ee9c4d77f135'::uuid, -- drawdown-improve-aquaculture
     'Check where the farmed fish at your store come from',
     'At a grocery store or fish counter, look at the labels on farmed fish and shellfish to see where they were raised and any farming certifications. Make a simple chart of what you found, and look up what one of the labels means, with a source. Post a photo of your chart.',
     'research', 'explore', 1, 100, 'review', array['observation','research']::text[]),
    ('da0a9a12-65d1-5a46-bcce-f359ebf13333'::uuid, -- drawdown-deploy-electric-irrigation-pumps
     'Explain how farms pump water without diesel',
     'Many farms pump irrigation water with diesel engines, while others use electric or solar-powered pumps. Read reliable sources about these choices and make a short explainer, poster or video in plain words. Post it with sources.',
     'education', 'create', 2, 100, 'review', array['research','teaching']::text[]),
    ('fabf57f7-bd14-5ec5-a980-41397329157a'::uuid, -- drawdown-improve-manure-management
     'Look up the manure storage rules for big farms',
     'Many places require permits for large livestock farms, including rules on how they store manure. Find those rules on your environmental agency''s website, and if it publishes permit records, look at a few from your county or region to see how manure storage is handled in practice. Write a short summary of what the rules require and what you noticed, describing farms in general terms. Post it with links.',
     'research', 'explore', 3, 150, 'review', array['research','data-analysis']::text[]),
    ('38f5c62c-a8cb-5ac4-b0b1-aba602a400d5'::uuid, -- drawdown-reduce-overfishing
     'Find out which fish stocks near you are healthy',
     'Look up your national or regional fisheries agency''s public reports on the status of fish stocks in your nearest waters, or for fish commonly sold where you live. Make a short, plain-language summary of which stocks the agency says are healthy and which are overfished, with links. Post it.',
     'research', 'explore', 2, 100, 'review', array['research','data-analysis']::text[]),
    ('b5a1b342-9b1c-537e-920b-98226ad45669'::uuid, -- drawdown-protect-seafloors
     'Map the protected areas of your nearest sea',
     'Use a public map of marine protected areas from your government or a reputable international database to find protected areas in the sea nearest you, and what activities, such as bottom trawling, are allowed there. Make a simple map or table with sources. Post it.',
     'research', 'explore', 2, 100, 'review', array['research','mapping']::text[]),
    ('dfb7d2eb-1373-59ae-bacd-22668b604f68'::uuid, -- drawdown-restore-grasslands-savannas
     'Make an ID card for local grassland plants',
     'Using a local native plant society, botanic garden or parks agency guide, choose a handful of native grasses and wildflowers that grow in grasslands near you. Make a simple identification card with your own photo or drawing and one fact for each, for hikers or a school group. Post a photo of your card.',
     'education', 'create', 1, 100, 'review', array['research','design']::text[]),
    ('74a7935a-731f-5f35-ad12-f1799e22d378'::uuid, -- drawdown-restore-mangrove-ecosystems
     'Draw a labeled picture of a mangrove forest',
     'Look at photos and diagrams from reliable sources, then draw or paint a mangrove forest showing its roots, the water and some of the animals that live there, with simple labels. Share it with a class, a youth group or online. Post a photo of your artwork with your sources.',
     'creative', 'create', 1, 100, 'review', array['drawing','research']::text[]),
    ('96685219-f741-5c38-97ad-cdc5eceba121'::uuid, -- drawdown-restore-salt-marsh-ecosystems
     'Join an organized marsh restoration or cleanup',
     'Find a volunteer day run by a park agency or conservation group that restores or cleans up a salt marsh or coastal shoreline, such as planting marsh grass or clearing trash, and join it. If you live far from the coast or nothing is scheduled this week, find a salt marsh restoration project online and share what it does and how people can help. Post a photo of your work or a link to where you shared the project.',
     'community', 'help', 2, 100, 'review', array['community','outdoors']::text[]),
    ('78ab0a5d-ca2b-52b2-a9d0-54827b5f3fd7'::uuid, -- drawdown-restore-seagrass-ecosystems
     'Make a seagrass care card for boaters',
     'Seagrass meadows can be damaged by boat propellers and anchors. Using official marine agency guidance, make a short, friendly card explaining how boaters, paddlers and swimmers can avoid harming seagrass, and ask a marina, shop or club whether you may post or hand it out. Post a photo of your card.',
     'education', 'create', 2, 100, 'review', array['design','writing']::text[]),
    ('a4f79ed1-4534-57fc-a181-33e95fc87b0c'::uuid, -- drawdown-restore-seaweed-ecosystems
     'Follow a kelp forest restoration project online',
     'Find a seaweed or kelp restoration project through a marine agency, university or conservation group, and follow its updates for a week. Write a short summary of what the project is doing and how volunteers or the public can get involved. Post it with links.',
     'research', 'explore', 1, 100, 'review', array['research','writing']::text[]),
    ('ff2a6de8-b97e-5642-acb6-25b39fcc4a9a'::uuid, -- drawdown-improve-fuel-burning-cooking-equipment
     'Make an explainer on cleaner cookstoves and fuels',
     'Read about cleaner cookstoves and cooking fuels from reliable public health and development sources. Make a short post, poster or video explaining what cleaner cooking means and why it matters to families who cook over open fires, and keep it respectful of cooking traditions. Post a link or photo of your explainer with your sources named.',
     'education', 'create', 2, 100, 'review', array['research','writing']::text[]),
    ('4f17538c-53b5-5c0e-9a9a-2d8ff007990f'::uuid, -- drawdown-deploy-electric-cooking-equipment
     'Share a recipe made only with plug-in appliances',
     'Cook a simple dish using only electric equipment, such as an electric or induction stove, a kettle, a rice cooker or a slow cooker. Write it up as a recipe card that people in small apartments or shared housing could follow, and share it with neighbors or a community group. Post a photo of the dish and the recipe card.',
     'creative', 'create', 1, 100, 'review', array['cooking','writing']::text[]),
    ('9991a89f-e662-599f-84d2-e13c725e139d'::uuid, -- drawdown-deploy-district-cooling
     'Draw how one plant can cool many buildings',
     'District cooling connects many buildings to one central source of chilled water for air conditioning. Read about it from reliable public sources, then draw a simple diagram or comic that shows how the cold water travels out and comes back. Post a photo of your drawing with the sources you used.',
     'creative', 'create', 2, 100, 'review', array['design','research']::text[]),
    ('728a63c6-8282-5cf3-91c6-90578935883d'::uuid, -- drawdown-deploy-micro-wind-turbines
     'Keep a week-long wind diary for your street',
     'For a week, check the wind near your home at the same times each day by watching flags, trees or a ribbon on your own balcony or fence, and compare what you see with the official weather forecast. At the end, write a few lines on whether the wind where you live is steady or gusty and why small turbines need good wind. Post a photo of your diary.',
     'research', 'explore', 1, 100, 'review', array['observation','data-analysis']::text[]),
    ('1bd34e77-5d56-532f-8989-77f1bde20630'::uuid, -- drawdown-deploy-nuclear-fusion
     'Explain fusion and fission in plain words',
     'Read a few reliable public sources, such as a national science agency or a university, about how nuclear fusion differs from the nuclear fission used in today''s power plants. Make a short post, poster or video that explains the difference in plain words, including what is still unknown, and list your sources. Post a link or photo.',
     'education', 'create', 2, 100, 'review', array['research','teaching']::text[]),
    ('9f545890-788e-5ce4-b6ce-042251b8d441'::uuid, -- drawdown-deploy-small-modular-nuclear-reactors
     'Check the public record on new reactor proposals',
     'Visit the public website of your country''s nuclear safety regulator, look for applications or plans for small modular reactors, and note any in your region. Write a short, neutral summary of what is proposed, where it stands, and any public meetings or comment periods. Post your summary with links.',
     'research', 'explore', 2, 100, 'review', array['research','policy-analysis']::text[]),
    ('f364102d-e11f-583a-8249-e8ce07615a75'::uuid, -- drawdown-deploy-advanced-geothermal-energy
     'Make a short video on next-generation geothermal',
     'Read about newer geothermal approaches, which aim to reach heat deep underground in places without natural hot springs, using reliable sources such as energy agencies and universities. Make a short video, slideshow or comic that explains the idea in plain words and what researchers are still testing. Post it with your sources listed.',
     'education', 'create', 2, 100, 'review', array['video','research']::text[]),
    ('1ba35152-acfa-5786-8eb7-015bfa01c232'::uuid, -- drawdown-deploy-methane-digesters
     'Find out if your wastewater plant makes biogas',
     'Look up the wastewater treatment plant that serves your area on its official website or annual report and see whether it uses digesters to turn sludge into biogas. If it isn''t clear, send a short question through the official contact form, or sign up for a public tour if one is offered. Post what you learned with links.',
     'research', 'explore', 2, 100, 'review', array['research','writing']::text[]),
    ('3fb16043-b210-577e-b662-670cb9df0296'::uuid, -- drawdown-improve-district-heating-industry
     'Ask your council about reusing waste heat',
     'Factories, data centers and wastewater plants often give off waste heat that could be piped to nearby factories and other buildings. Check your city or regional energy or climate plan for any mention of waste heat or heat networks for industry, then send a polite question in your own words to a council member or planning office asking whether this has been studied locally. Post your question, any reply and links to what you read, with names and contact details hidden.',
     'advocacy', 'create', 2, 100, 'review', array['policy-analysis','writing']::text[]),
    ('29222f7a-28ca-54ba-970f-bbef5c525b0f'::uuid, -- drawdown-deploy-plastic-alternatives-bioplastics
     'Find out if your town takes compostable plastics',
     'Look at your local waste agency''s official recycling and compost rules to see whether compostable or plant-based plastics are accepted, and where they should go. Make a short, clear post or sign so neighbors don''t have to guess. Post a photo or link with the official source.',
     'education', 'create', 1, 100, 'review', array['research','writing']::text[]),
    ('940d2140-eb2f-58dc-b798-4ffc96fff671'::uuid, -- drawdown-improve-steel-production
     'Make a timeline of steelmaking, past to present',
     'Research how steel has been made, from early furnaces to today''s electric furnaces and newer methods that use hydrogen and clean power, using museums, libraries or reliable websites. If your region has a steel history, include it. Make a simple illustrated timeline and post a photo or link with your sources.',
     'research', 'create', 2, 100, 'review', array['research','design']::text[]),
    ('154bc628-8758-51ed-924a-1dd61ed2e171'::uuid, -- drawdown-reduce-airplane-contrails
     'Keep a week-long sky diary of plane trails',
     'For a week, look up at the same times each day and note the plane trails you see: do they fade quickly or spread out into thin clouds? Read a reliable source on why some trails linger, and add a short note. Post a photo of your diary or a few sky photos.',
     'research', 'explore', 1, 100, 'review', array['observation','photography']::text[]),
    ('4a35883c-a97e-5422-bd31-c5a6e4763554'::uuid, -- drawdown-mobilize-green-hydrogen-for-aviation-and-trucking
     'Weigh up hydrogen-powered trucks and planes',
     'Read reliable sources about using green hydrogen, made with renewable electricity, to power long-haul trucks and planes. Make a fair pros-and-cons chart in plain words, noting what is already working and what is still being tested. Post it with sources.',
     'research', 'create', 2, 100, 'review', array['research','writing']::text[]),
    ('12db7169-9d11-5a35-988c-d58c8d0a3c86'::uuid, -- drawdown-deploy-sustainable-aviation-fuel
     'Check one airline''s claims about cleaner jet fuel',
     'Find an airline''s public statements about sustainable aviation fuel, such as a press release or sustainability report. List what they say, then check reliable independent sources for what is known about that kind of fuel, and write a short, fair summary. Post it with links.',
     'research', 'explore', 2, 100, 'review', array['research','writing']::text[]),
    ('0f2c4e86-82a9-5e77-9998-68ddb3c337fa'::uuid, -- drawdown-advance-cultivated-meat
     'Ask people what they think of cultivated meat',
     'Ask a few friends, relatives or classmates whether they would try meat grown from animal cells instead of from a slaughtered animal, and why. Keep answers anonymous and write a short summary of the range of views. Post your summary.',
     'research', 'explore', 1, 100, 'review', array['interviewing','writing']::text[]),
    ('22458ffa-9f2e-5a40-b72f-921a3a09b5a0'::uuid, -- drawdown-use-feed-additives
     'Explain cow burps and climate in a short video',
     'Cattle, sheep and goats release methane mostly by burping as they digest grass. Read reliable sources about the feed additives researchers are testing to cut that methane, then make a short video, comic or post that explains the idea and what is still being studied. Post it with sources.',
     'education', 'create', 1, 100, 'review', array['video','research']::text[]),
    ('a67c7c74-c7f6-55fc-b546-3ea4b959745a'::uuid, -- drawdown-improve-irrigation-water-use-efficiency
     'Track rainfall with a jar to guide your watering',
     'Set a straight-sided jar or can on the ground in an open spot and check it each day for a week to see how much rain has fallen. Use what you see to decide when your garden, balcony plants or community plot really need watering, and note each time you watered. Post a photo of your jar and your notes.',
     'research', 'explore', 1, 100, 'review', array['observation','gardening']::text[]),
    ('f9085849-2b32-5436-8bbe-99e52ed4e57b'::uuid, -- drawdown-deploy-leaf-protein-concentrates
     'Make a fact sheet on protein made from leaves',
     'Read reliable sources about leaf protein, which is protein taken from green leaves and crop leftovers for use in food and animal feed. Make a one-page fact sheet that explains how it is made and what researchers are still working out. Post a photo or link with your sources.',
     'education', 'create', 2, 100, 'review', array['research','writing']::text[]),
    ('f3e231f6-139d-504b-952e-b7deb39f9422'::uuid, -- drawdown-improve-ruminant-breeding
     'Watch and summarize a talk on cattle breeding',
     'Find a free public talk, webinar or lecture video from a university or agricultural agency about breeding cattle or sheep that produce less methane. Watch it and write a short summary in plain words of what you learned and what questions remain. Post your summary with a link to the talk.',
     'education', 'explore', 1, 100, 'review', array['research','writing']::text[]),
    ('ffc85842-a7a4-5629-a9c1-8b41a58eb5c1'::uuid, -- drawdown-deploy-seaweed-farming-for-food
     'Cook a dish with store-bought seaweed',
     'Buy a small pack of edible seaweed from a grocery store, such as nori or kelp, and make a simple dish with it. Share the recipe along with a few facts about how seaweed is farmed in the ocean, with your source. Post a photo of your dish and the recipe.',
     'creative', 'create', 1, 100, 'review', array['cooking','research']::text[]),
    ('93e0f0e8-0fe4-59f7-907f-05ac7287a250'::uuid, -- drawdown-deploy-alternative-grazing
     'Ask a farm advisor how local herds are grazed',
     'Contact your local agricultural advisory service, a university farm program or a grazing association with a short question: what grazing methods do local farmers use, such as moving animals often between fenced areas so the grass can rest? Write a plain-language summary of the answer or of their published guides. Post your summary with sources.',
     'research', 'explore', 2, 100, 'review', array['research','interviewing']::text[]),
    ('1a9c8fcb-2a76-56de-b019-9c1f23a19800'::uuid, -- drawdown-deploy-enhanced-rock-weathering
     'Explain how crushed rock can absorb carbon',
     'Some rocks slowly react with carbon dioxide as they break down, and spreading crushed rock on fields could speed this up. Read reliable sources, then make a short explainer, comic or video in plain words, including what is still being tested. Post it with sources.',
     'education', 'create', 2, 100, 'review', array['research','teaching']::text[]),
    ('2bab59bf-f317-5962-bdaa-2ee1ebbb664a'::uuid, -- drawdown-reduce-grazing-intensity
     'Explain why grazed land needs time to rest',
     'Read reliable sources about what happens to grassland when too many animals graze it for too long, and how fewer animals or longer rest periods let plants and soil recover. Make a short explainer, comic or poster in plain words. Post it with your sources.',
     'education', 'create', 1, 100, 'review', array['research','teaching']::text[]),
    ('3f646f9c-5619-54ed-b38a-3977d359c61c'::uuid, -- drawdown-restore-large-herbivores
     'Find out which big grazers once roamed your region',
     'Research which large plant-eating animals, such as bison, elk or others, once lived in your region and whether any are being brought back. Make a poster or post with what you found, including what scientists are still unsure about. Post it with your sources.',
     'research', 'create', 2, 100, 'review', array['research','design']::text[]),
    ('3933adb5-41e2-57fc-9f40-a2cf8f7ab0f4'::uuid, -- drawdown-deploy-ocean-alkalinity-enhancement
     'Write a fair explainer on changing seawater chemistry',
     'Read reliable sources about ocean alkalinity enhancement, which means adding certain minerals to seawater so it can take up more carbon dioxide. Write a short, balanced explainer that covers how it works, what field studies are testing and what concerns people have raised. Post it with sources.',
     'research', 'create', 2, 100, 'review', array['research','writing']::text[]),
    ('9f0aea98-532e-5160-8e48-eb1f76dcea68'::uuid, -- drawdown-deploy-ocean-electrochemistry
     'Gather your questions about ocean carbon removal',
     'Read an introduction to ocean electrochemistry, which uses electricity to change seawater so it can help remove carbon dioxide, from a university or agency source. Write down your own questions about it, then look for answers in reliable sources and note which ones are still open. Post your questions and answers with sources.',
     'research', 'explore', 2, 100, 'review', array['research','writing']::text[]),
    ('747455c5-6ce7-5aa0-9363-e3dd41f8e954'::uuid, -- drawdown-restore-whale-populations
     'Write a short kids'' story about whales',
     'Read about whales from reliable sources, such as an aquarium, museum or marine agency, including how whaling once cut their numbers and how some populations are recovering. Write a short story or picture-book page for kids that shares one true fact. Post your story with your sources.',
     'creative', 'create', 1, 100, 'review', array['writing','research']::text[]),
    ('91846487-707c-509d-b421-488fcd896853'::uuid, -- drawdown-bury-biomass
     'Find out what happens to your town''s yard waste',
     'Check your local waste agency''s website to learn where leaves, branches and other yard waste go after collection, such as composting, mulching, burning or landfill. Write a short summary, and add a note with a source on the idea of storing carbon by burying wood so it can''t rot. Post it with links.',
     'research', 'explore', 1, 100, 'review', array['research','writing']::text[]),
    ('7f666cb5-019d-5542-9809-9f8e606e13ab'::uuid, -- drawdown-use-methane-oxidizing-coatings
     'Explain methane in plain words',
     'Make a short explainer, poster or video about methane: where it comes from, why it matters for the climate, and new ideas researchers are testing to break it down, such as special coatings on roofs. Use reliable sources and list them. Post it.',
     'education', 'create', 1, 100, 'review', array['research','teaching']::text[]),
    ('4038956a-ca7c-562f-91bd-3503247de3cf'::uuid, -- drawdown-manage-coal-mine-methane
     'Map coal mines in your region using public data',
     'Use public data, such as your government''s mining records or a reputable open database of coal mines, to find coal mines in your region or country, including closed ones. Note whether any public rules or reports mention capturing the methane gas that escapes from mines, and make a short map or table with sources. Post it.',
     'research', 'explore', 3, 150, 'review', array['research','data-analysis','mapping']::text[]),
    ('a14f8bcc-20bc-5624-b7af-1105cfcea5e5'::uuid, -- drawdown-manage-oil-gas-methane
     'Write a public comment on oil and gas methane',
     'Look through official sources, such as your environmental agency''s rulemaking page or the government''s public comment portal, for an open proposal about methane leaks from oil and gas operations. Read the plain-language summary and write a short, respectful comment in your own words, then submit it, or save it as a draft if nothing is open right now. Post a link or screenshot with personal details hidden.',
     'advocacy', 'create', 3, 150, 'review', array['policy-analysis','writing']::text[]),
    ('472f9ccf-b9cd-5567-84e0-fb00b634e3ec'::uuid, -- drawdown-use-nitrous-oxide-removal
     'Explain nitrous oxide''s role in climate change',
     'Nitrous oxide is a powerful greenhouse gas, and most of the nitrous oxide that people add to the air comes from farming, especially fertilizer use, with smaller shares from industry and other sources. Read reliable sources and make a short explainer, poster or video about where it comes from and the early research into removing it from the air. Post it with sources.',
     'education', 'create', 2, 100, 'review', array['research','teaching']::text[]),
    ('f28ecf0f-2992-5816-96aa-51e8c71aad36'::uuid, -- drawdown-deploy-concentrated-solar
     'Explain the two main kinds of solar power',
     'Learn the difference between solar panels, which turn sunlight straight into electricity, and concentrated solar plants, which use mirrors to focus sunlight into heat that drives a generator. Make a simple poster, comic or post that shows both side by side, with sources. Post a photo or link.',
     'education', 'create', 1, 100, 'review', array['design','teaching']::text[]),
    ('ce76cfb0-b91f-54cf-bf86-12f19f3721e8'::uuid, -- drawdown-deploy-geothermal-power
     'Map geothermal energy sites in your region',
     'Use public maps from a geological survey or energy agency to find geothermal power plants, hot springs or underground heat resources in your region, or the nearest ones if there are none close by. Mark them on a simple map and add a sentence on how geothermal power uses heat from underground. Post your map with sources.',
     'research', 'explore', 2, 100, 'review', array['research','mapping']::text[]),
    ('cc530601-de9e-5e1a-a527-6c0c3b406ed8'::uuid, -- drawdown-improve-grid-efficiency
     'Ask your utility a public question about the grid',
     'Find your electric utility''s most recent public plan for its grid, often called a long-term resource plan or grid upgrade plan, on its website or your energy regulator''s website. Write one clear question about how it plans to cut the power lost along its wires, and send it through the official comment or contact channel. Post your question and any reply.',
     'advocacy', 'create', 2, 100, 'review', array['policy-analysis','writing']::text[]),
    ('7d91c8c4-dfde-5a47-a4eb-8a9cc2b5f164'::uuid, -- drawdown-deploy-nuclear-power
     'Chart where your home''s electricity comes from',
     'Find your electricity supplier''s fuel mix, which is often published in a yearly disclosure, printed on bills or shown on a government energy website, and see how much comes from nuclear, gas, coal, wind, solar and other sources. Turn it into a simple pie chart or drawing and share it with your household or neighbors. Post a photo of your chart and the source.',
     'research', 'explore', 1, 100, 'review', array['research','data-analysis']::text[]),
    ('57d485fb-678b-59df-ac98-1bf8e967151d'::uuid, -- drawdown-boost-industrial-efficiency
     'Profile a local business that cuts its energy use',
     'Ask a small local business, such as a bakery, print shop or workshop, whether they have done anything to use less energy, like changing equipment schedules or fixing leaks. With the owner''s permission, write a short profile of what they did and why. Post the profile with any photos they agreed to.',
     'business', 'explore', 2, 100, 'review', array['interviewing','writing']::text[]),
    ('84e494bd-6005-53d1-bd0e-118464f74006'::uuid, -- drawdown-increase-industrial-electrification
     'List the large industrial sites near you',
     'Use a public pollution or emissions database from your national environmental agency to list the large industrial facilities in your area, what they make and, where the database says, which fuels they burn for heat. Turn it into a simple map or table so neighbors know what is nearby. Post it with links to the source.',
     'research', 'explore', 2, 100, 'review', array['research','data-analysis','mapping']::text[]),
    ('fbc5cefc-3a2a-5248-b1ea-4ce33c7f68de'::uuid, -- drawdown-deploy-low-emission-industrial-feedstocks
     'Trace the raw materials of an everyday product',
     'Pick an everyday item, such as a plastic bottle, a bag of fertilizer or a cleaning product, and use reliable sources to find out what raw materials it starts from and how they are processed. Draw a simple flow chart from raw material to the item in your hands. Post a photo of your chart with sources.',
     'research', 'create', 2, 100, 'review', array['research','design']::text[]),
    ('b873229b-271c-5d8f-8aae-a8ca6f48adb9'::uuid, -- drawdown-improve-other-building-materials
     'Photograph the building materials on a local street',
     'Walk along a public street you like, such as a main street or a road by a park; it doesn''t have to be your own. Take close-up photos of the materials you can see in buildings and walls, such as brick, wood, concrete, stone, steel and glass. Make a labeled collage, and add a note with a source on one material that builders are trying to make with less pollution. Post the collage.',
     'creative', 'explore', 1, 100, 'review', array['photography','research']::text[]),
    ('b6b35fdf-9966-5375-81a8-06dfb8210d90'::uuid, -- drawdown-improve-aviation-efficiency
     'Read your nearest airport''s climate plan',
     'Find your nearest airport''s sustainability or climate plan on its official website. Write a short, plain-language summary of what it says about saving fuel and cutting emissions on the ground and in the air, and list one question you still have. Post your summary with a link.',
     'research', 'explore', 2, 100, 'review', array['research','writing']::text[]),
    ('746f7501-6f2e-53ac-9b95-695dfa524285'::uuid, -- drawdown-mobilize-electric-buses
     'Ask your transit agency about its bus fleet plans',
     'Find your transit agency''s public plans for its buses, such as a fleet plan or board meeting materials, and check whether electric buses are part of them. Send a short public question or comment through the official channel or at a public meeting, mentioning the routes that matter to your neighbors. Post your question and any reply.',
     'advocacy', 'create', 2, 100, 'review', array['policy-analysis','writing']::text[]),
    ('5990d682-73e8-51a3-9d48-620b2c3709ba'::uuid, -- drawdown-mobilize-electric-trains
     'Find out how the trains in your region run',
     'Using your rail operator''s or transport agency''s public information, find out which train lines in your region run on electricity and which run on diesel. Draw a simple map or chart, and add any plans to electrify more lines. Post it with sources.',
     'research', 'explore', 2, 100, 'review', array['research','mapping']::text[]),
    ('3ef1924b-6179-5090-8b0c-c0ae158439c5'::uuid, -- drawdown-mobilize-electric-trucks
     'Map truck routes that pass schools and parks',
     'Find your city''s or region''s official truck route map, or note from a safe spot where delivery and freight trucks travel near you. Mark where those routes pass schools, parks or homes, and add any public plans for cleaner delivery trucks. Post your map with sources.',
     'research', 'explore', 2, 100, 'review', array['mapping','research']::text[]),
    ('dbbbf58e-d51e-5a68-b40e-64267511c8e1'::uuid, -- drawdown-enhance-high-speed-rail
     'Plan a trip by train instead of a short flight',
     'Pick a trip you or your family might take that people usually fly, and plan how you could make it by train instead, using official rail operator websites. Write up the route, the connections and the door-to-door travel time compared with flying. Post your plan; you don''t have to book anything.',
     'research', 'explore', 1, 100, 'review', array['research','planning']::text[]),
    ('f9ca7b5a-ce23-5eab-a159-c2a5f5474256'::uuid, -- drawdown-improve-ocean-shipping-efficiency
     'Follow one cargo ship''s voyage for a week',
     'Use a free public ship-tracking website to pick one container ship or cargo ship and check on it each day for a week. Note where it goes, how fast it travels and which ports it visits, then write a short post about what you learned about global shipping. Post screenshots and your notes.',
     'research', 'explore', 1, 100, 'review', array['research','observation']::text[]),
    ('672ab8e1-4259-500a-8c6d-60fab989f0af'::uuid, -- drawdown-improve-supply-chain-efficiency
     'Map where a week of your groceries comes from',
     'For a week, check the labels on the groceries your household buys to see where each item was grown or made. Mark the places on a map and note which items came from nearby and which traveled far. Post a photo or screenshot of your map.',
     'research', 'explore', 1, 100, 'review', array['mapping','observation']::text[]),
    ('ad54f184-7484-5ce2-827b-c431a13b6112'::uuid, -- drawdown-improve-truck-efficiency
     'Share your area''s rules on vehicle idling',
     'Look up whether your city, state or country has official rules on leaving engines running while parked, often called anti-idling rules. Make a short, friendly post or flyer with the official link, especially for places like school pickup lines or loading zones. Post a photo or link of what you shared.',
     'education', 'create', 1, 100, 'review', array['research','writing']::text[]),
    ('2ef53c00-7044-51b7-88c5-d5f3b4acd312'::uuid, -- drawdown-hold-virtual-meetings
     'Teach someone to join a video call',
     'Help a neighbor, relative or community group member who isn''t comfortable with video calls learn to join one, so they can take part in meetings without traveling. Use a free, well-known app on their own device and practice with a short test call. Post a short note or photo of your session, with their permission.',
     'mutual_aid', 'help', 1, 100, 'review', array['teaching','mutual_aid']::text[]),
    ('0cd5b19c-24c0-5104-833e-3342d928d644'::uuid, -- drawdown-improve-forest-management
     'Share your community''s wildfire plan in plain words',
     'Look up your area''s official wildfire or forest plan, such as a community wildfire protection plan, on your local fire department, forest agency or emergency management website. Summarize the main points in plain words and link to the official preparedness guidance; if your area has no wildfire plan, summarize the management plan for a nearby public forest instead. Post your summary.',
     'education', 'create', 2, 100, 'review', array['research','writing']::text[]),
    ('bada6edd-da39-5432-8371-787826da1ae9'::uuid, -- drawdown-deploy-precision-fermentation
     'Explain how microbes can brew food ingredients',
     'Precision fermentation uses microbes like yeast to make specific food ingredients, such as proteins found in milk or eggs. Read reliable sources and make a short explainer, comic or video comparing it with familiar fermentation like bread or yogurt. Post it with your sources.',
     'education', 'create', 2, 100, 'review', array['research','teaching']::text[]),
    ('3dff93b8-f019-504d-86fa-bf2149494a7b'::uuid, -- drawdown-manage-increase-urban-trees
     'Map the shade trees along a few local blocks',
     'Walk a few blocks you know well on the sidewalk, such as near a park, school or main street, and map the street trees and shady spots, noting bus stops, playgrounds and benches with no shade. Check whether your city has a program for requesting a street tree, and share it with neighbors. Post your map and the program link.',
     'advocacy', 'explore', 1, 100, 'review', array['mapping','observation']::text[]),
    ('bec0d368-558d-5579-85a3-94f0bf1a4aff'::uuid, -- drawdown-restore-abandoned-farmland
     'Compare old and new maps of farmland near you',
     'Use a free online archive of old maps or aerial photos and compare it with a current map of an area near you. Mark places that used to be farmed and are now turning back into woods, meadow or something else. Post side-by-side screenshots with your notes.',
     'research', 'explore', 2, 100, 'review', array['mapping','research']::text[]),
    ('a8058210-5be8-5931-b1d1-8eddbe6d233c'::uuid, -- drawdown-deploy-agroforestry
     'Visit a public food forest or orchard',
     'Find a food forest, community orchard or farm that welcomes visitors and grows trees together with crops, and spend some time there learning how the layers of plants work together. If there isn''t one near you, find one online and make a short explainer instead. Post a photo essay or your explainer.',
     'research', 'explore', 1, 100, 'review', array['observation','photography']::text[]),
    ('4c8ab486-7307-5931-b7e9-c52f39621ee8'::uuid, -- drawdown-deploy-biomass-crops-on-degraded-land
     'Map vacant and worn-out land in your area',
     'Use public maps, city records or land-use data to find vacant lots, old industrial land or worn-out farmland in your area. Make a simple map and note which sites, if any, have public plans for new uses. Post your map with sources.',
     'research', 'explore', 2, 100, 'review', array['mapping','research']::text[]),
    ('a4b81a7c-fb6d-514a-b374-44257864fa4a'::uuid, -- drawdown-deploy-perennial-crops
     'Map fruit and nut trees in public spaces',
     'Walk through parks, public paths and the planting strips along streets, and map the fruit and nut trees and other plants that produce food year after year, leaving trees in private yards off the map. Check whether a local group or the land manager allows public picking, and note it on your map. Post your map.',
     'research', 'explore', 1, 100, 'review', array['mapping','observation']::text[]),
    ('43870b45-575d-5eab-a8ab-62dff97cbd64'::uuid, -- drawdown-deploy-heat-pump-water-heaters
     'Find out what heats your home''s hot water',
     'Look for the label on your home''s water heater, if you can see it without moving anything, to find out whether it runs on gas, electricity or a heat pump. If you rent and can''t see it, ask your landlord or building manager. Post a short note on what you learned, with a photo of the label if you have one.',
     'education', 'explore', 1, 100, 'review', array['observation','research']::text[]),
    ('480815e2-a8a7-5ffa-9365-7c7c6144bb5a'::uuid, -- drawdown-deploy-solar-hot-water-heaters
     'Run a sunshine water-warming demo',
     'On a sunny day, fill two plastic bottles with water, wrap one in black paper or cloth, and leave both in the sun for a few hours. Feel the difference, or check with a kitchen thermometer, and explain how solar water heaters use the same idea to warm water for homes. Post a photo or short video of your demo and what you noticed; it works well with kids.',
     'education', 'create', 1, 100, 'review', array['teaching','video']::text[]),
    ('c0b0ff89-2db0-5cfd-b384-3498c60fcd39'::uuid, -- drawdown-increase-building-deconstruction-recycling
     'Map where to find reused building materials',
     'Find the stores, salvage yards and swap groups near you that sell or give away used building materials, such as doors, tiles, lumber and fixtures. Put them on a simple map or list with hours and a link for each, so neighbors fixing up a home on a tight budget know where to look. Post your map or list.',
     'community', 'explore', 1, 100, 'review', array['research','mapping']::text[]),
    ('39bd46c7-59ff-5ae0-9149-8286497cb6bf'::uuid, -- drawdown-deploy-ocean-power
     'Make a kids'' quiz about power from waves and tides',
     'Read about how waves and tides can be used to make electricity from reliable sources, then write a short, friendly quiz for kids with an answer sheet. Try it with a young relative, a class or a youth group if you can. Post a photo or copy of your quiz and answers.',
     'education', 'create', 1, 100, 'review', array['teaching','writing']::text[]),
    ('9feafb02-8fcc-56b9-a896-b99512fbcd8a'::uuid, -- drawdown-deploy-small-hydropower
     'Map the dams and small hydro plants near you',
     'Use public maps or databases from your water or energy agency to find dams and small hydropower plants on rivers near you. Mark them on a simple map and note which ones make electricity, if the source says so. Post your map with source links.',
     'research', 'explore', 2, 100, 'review', array['research','mapping']::text[]),
    ('0dad8ffa-ebfd-50b2-b614-0dceb7c34565'::uuid, -- drawdown-deploy-utility-scale-hydropower
     'Tell the story of a big dam in your region',
     'Choose a large dam in your region or country and read published sources about it, including the power it provides and how it affected people and rivers upstream and downstream. Write a short, balanced story or timeline that includes more than one point of view, and list your sources. Post it.',
     'research', 'create', 2, 100, 'review', array['research','writing']::text[]),
    ('d517b83f-d4ab-5908-890d-fbe2dbf883b3'::uuid, -- drawdown-deploy-bioelectricity-with-carbon-capture-storage
     'Write a fair Q&A on bioenergy with carbon capture',
     'Read reliable sources about making power from plants or plant waste while capturing the carbon dioxide and storing it underground. Write a short question-and-answer sheet that covers how it works, what supporters hope for and what critics worry about, with sources. Post it.',
     'research', 'create', 2, 100, 'review', array['research','writing']::text[]),
    ('2c835624-5420-5c50-b650-aa4c318a596b'::uuid, -- drawdown-deploy-advanced-biofuels
     'Make a plain-words guide to biofuels',
     'Read reliable sources about the different kinds of biofuels, from those made from food crops to newer ones made from waste oils and farm leftovers. Make a short guide or chart that explains the differences and the open questions in plain words. Post it with sources.',
     'education', 'create', 2, 100, 'review', array['research','writing']::text[]),
    ('66d427db-388f-5c92-97c5-6598d8490a0d'::uuid, -- drawdown-improve-routing-logistics
     'Team up with a neighbor to combine errands',
     'Plan your errands for the week as one efficient loop, and offer to pick up a few things for a neighbor who has trouble getting out, so one trip does the job of two. Agree clearly on what you''ll pick up and how it will be paid for, and keep the receipts. Post a short note on how it went, without names, addresses or your route.',
     'mutual_aid', 'help', 1, 100, 'review', array['mutual_aid','planning']::text[]),
    ('4357d930-c114-5e45-a22c-335b9eab43d4'::uuid, -- drawdown-produce-bio-oils
     'Explain storing carbon in oil made from plant waste',
     'Some companies heat plant waste without oxygen to make a thick bio-oil, then store it deep underground to keep its carbon out of the air. Read reliable sources and make a short, balanced explainer of how it works and what questions remain. Post it with sources.',
     'education', 'create', 2, 100, 'review', array['research','writing']::text[]),
    ('3c32fd6a-1abe-569f-a395-c4309d76d301'::uuid, -- drawdown-deploy-clean-cooking
     'Ask an elder how your family used to cook',
     'Ask a parent, grandparent or older neighbor how meals were cooked when they were young: what fuel they used, where the smoke went and how cooking has changed since. Write down or record their story with their permission. Post a short write-up or audio clip.',
     'research', 'explore', 1, 100, 'review', array['interviewing','writing']::text[])
  ) as v(id, title, description, domain, discovery_category, difficulty, base_points, verification_mode, skills)
on conflict (id) do nothing;

-- --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 2. their 125 details rows: proof hint, safety note, credit, quotation, source, licence
insert into public.action_mission_details
  (mission_id, catalog, slug, proof_hint, safety_note, credit_line, about, about_credit, source_url,
   license_name, license_url, doi)
select v.mission_id, 'drawdown', v.slug, v.proof_hint, v.safety_note, v.credit_line, v.about, v.about_credit,
       v.source_url, v.license_name, v.license_url, v.doi
  from (values
    ('237b2be1-b651-5f68-9af3-f26076bb823b'::uuid, 'drawdown-deploy-alternative-insulation-materials',
     'A photo of your comparison chart, with product types and what each is made of.',
     'Look at packaging and product sheets only; don''t open packages or handle loose fibers, which can irritate skin and lungs.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/deploy-alternative-insulation-materials), used with permission; assessment "Deploy Alternative Insulation Materials- Solution Assessment Spreadsheet" by Sarah Gleeson, https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21231150, licensed CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'Deploy Alternative Insulation Materials is defined as using alternative building insulation materials in place of conventional ones. In particular, we highlight the impact of using cellulose instead of glass, mineral, or plastic insulation in new and retrofit buildings.',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/deploy-alternative-insulation-materials', 'CC BY 4.0', 'https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/', 'https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21231150'),
    ('c44d0a0d-1c7f-5396-a071-80149e36c664'::uuid, 'drawdown-deploy-alternative-refrigerants',
     'A photo of the refrigerant label with your short note.',
     'Read only labels you can see easily; don''t move heavy appliances, unplug them or touch any tubing or sealed parts.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/deploy-alternative-refrigerants), used with permission; assessment "Deploy Alternative Refrigerants- Solutions Assessment Spreadsheet" by Sarah Gleeson and Heather McDiarmid, https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21246134, licensed CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'This solution involves reducing the use of high-global warming potential (GWP) refrigerants, instead deploying lower-GWP refrigerants. High-GWP (>800 on a 100-yr basis) fluorinated gases (F-gases) are currently used as refrigerants in refrigeration, air conditioning, and heat pump systems. Over the lifetime of this equipment, refrigerants escape into the atmosphere where they contribute to climate change.',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/deploy-alternative-refrigerants', 'CC BY 4.0', 'https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/', 'https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21246134'),
    ('169089fe-4e2c-54b5-a91f-11fcde81d44d'::uuid, 'drawdown-improve-refrigerant-management',
     'A link or photo of your post or flyer with the official sources listed.',
     'Never cut, drain or vent refrigerant lines yourself, since only trained, certified technicians should handle refrigerant, and put up flyers only where you have permission.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/improve-refrigerant-management), used with permission. Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'Improving refrigerant management involves deploying practices and technologies that reduce the amount of climate-warming refrigerant chemicals escaping into the atmosphere from air conditioning, refrigeration, and heat pump equipment. This solution has two components: reducing refrigerant leaks during refrigerant charging and use, and recovering refrigerant to prevent its release from end-of-life equipment.',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/improve-refrigerant-management', null, null, null),
    ('7bf1aab9-7278-547d-810b-df442bb1eb04'::uuid, 'drawdown-deploy-building-automation-systems',
     'A screenshot or photo of your question and any answer, with names and contact details removed.',
     'Ask only through official public channels, and never enter staff-only areas or touch any controls or equipment.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/deploy-building-automation-systems), used with permission; assessment "Deploy Building Automation Systems- Solution Assessment Spreadsheet" by Heather McDiarmid and Henry Igugu, https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21876968, licensed CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'We define Deploy Building Automation Systems (BASs) as reducing commercial (i.e., nonresidential or industrial) building energy use and associated GHG emissions by using sensors to monitor a building in operation and control systems such as heating, cooling, ventilation, plug loads, and lighting for the purpose of saving energy.',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/deploy-building-automation-systems', 'CC BY 4.0', 'https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/', 'https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21876968'),
    ('72c015b4-1c69-50d5-adee-2264d5fd2a53'::uuid, 'drawdown-improve-district-heating-buildings',
     'Your explainer with a map and source links.',
     'Use public documents and maps only, and don''t enter plant grounds, tunnels or utility areas.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/improve-district-heating-buildings), used with permission; assessment "Improve District Heating Buildings- Solution Assessment Spreadsheet" by Heather McDiarmid and Henry Igugu, https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23965820, licensed CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'A district heating system provides space and water heating to a large number of buildings through an underground distribution system.',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/improve-district-heating-buildings', 'CC BY 4.0', 'https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/', 'https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23965820'),
    ('bcf5b9c7-0423-5586-8fba-06b57be0ff19'::uuid, 'drawdown-use-heat-pumps',
     'A short write-up or audio clip of the interview, shared with the person''s permission.',
     'Share only what the person agrees to, and don''t give buying, financing or installation advice.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/use-heat-pumps), used with permission; assessment "Use Heat Pumps- Solution Assessment Spreadsheet" by Heather McDiarmid and Jason Lam, https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21246268, licensed CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'Heat pumps use electricity to efficiently move heat from one place to another. This solution focuses on the replacement of fossil fuel–based heating systems with electric heat pumps.',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/use-heat-pumps', 'CC BY 4.0', 'https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/', 'https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21246268'),
    ('02f26a02-9e16-50ff-aa3a-ff108aa9756c'::uuid, 'drawdown-use-smart-programmable-thermostats',
     'A short note on what you set up together, or a photo of the thermostat, with no schedule times, names or addresses showing.',
     'Change settings only with the resident present and agreeing, never ask for or type in their passwords, never open the device or touch wiring, and keep the home warm or cool enough for babies, older adults and anyone who is unwell.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/use-smart-programmable-thermostats), used with permission; assessment "Use Smart and Programmable Thermostats- Solution Assessment Spreadsheet" by Heather McDiarmid and Henry Igugu, https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22002791, licensed CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'We define Use Smart & Programmable Thermostats as reducing energy use and associated GHG emissions from heating and cooling by automatically making adjustments to the set temperature of a residential building.',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/use-smart-programmable-thermostats', 'CC BY 4.0', 'https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/', 'https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22002791'),
    ('8d7a5b07-2074-56b3-8355-47f79877d568'::uuid, 'drawdown-improve-windows-glass',
     'A photo of your sketch or list showing which windows have drafts.',
     'Use a tissue strip rather than a candle or lighter, and stay on the floor instead of climbing to reach high windows.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/improve-windows-glass), used with permission; assessment "Improve Windows and Glass- Solution Assessment Spreadsheet" by Henry Igugu and Sarah Gleeson, https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21246202, licensed CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'We define Improve Windows & Glass as reducing the heat transferred through typical windows used in residential and nonresidential buildings by improving the thermal insulation capacity of the glass. Windows typically constitute a small portion of a building envelope but account for a substantial portion of the heat transferred (gained or lost) between the indoor space and the external environment.',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/improve-windows-glass', 'CC BY 4.0', 'https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/', 'https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21246202'),
    ('0cab1dcb-56e2-501d-87e4-bee9130bf456'::uuid, 'drawdown-deploy-agrivoltaics',
     'A short written summary of the conversations, shared with permission.',
     'Ask politely, accept no for an answer, and share names, photos or farm details only with permission.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/deploy-agrivoltaics), used with permission; assessment "Deploy Agrivoltaics- Solutions Assessment Spreadsheet" by Al-Amin Bugaje and Megan Matthews, https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23769996, licensed CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'Agrivoltaics is the dual use of land for simultaneous solar photovoltaic (PV) power generation and agricultural production. It reduces GHG emissions by shifting electricity production from fossil fuels to renewables. Agrivoltaic systems can be categorized by system type, PV configuration, module tilt, and agricultural activity. These systems operate at both utility and distributed scales.',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/deploy-agrivoltaics', 'CC BY 4.0', 'https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/', 'https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23769996'),
    ('14a40713-7381-5a28-8506-03b4df42f043'::uuid, 'drawdown-deploy-distributed-solar-pv',
     'Your summary with official links, and where you shared it.',
     'Link only to official sources, and don''t recommend specific companies, contracts or financial deals.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/deploy-distributed-solar-pv), used with permission; assessment "Deploy Distributed Solar PV- Solution Assessment Spreadsheet" by Michael Dioha and Megan Matthews, https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21246308, licensed CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'Distributed solar photovoltaic (PV) systems are small-scale solar PV systems – usually under 1 MW, and installed near the point of use, such as on homes, businesses, or local facilities – that generate electricity for on-site consumption or local grid supply. This solution reduces reliance on centralized fossil-fuel power, cutting GHG emissions and minimizing transmission losses.',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/deploy-distributed-solar-pv', 'CC BY 4.0', 'https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/', 'https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21246308'),
    ('ba11cd9a-9260-548e-b5ef-93ff0f0445db'::uuid, 'drawdown-deploy-led-lighting',
     'A photo of your room-by-room tally.',
     'Check only bulbs that are switched off and cool, don''t climb, and don''t unscrew bulbs or open fixtures.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/deploy-led-lighting), used with permission; assessment "Deploy LED Lighting- Solution Assessment Spreadsheet" by Henry Igugu and Megan Matthews, https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21246185, licensed CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'We define the Deploy LED Lighting solution as replacing energy-inefficient light sources with light-emitting diodes (LEDs).',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/deploy-led-lighting', 'CC BY 4.0', 'https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/', 'https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21246185'),
    ('82ce9fb9-9081-5523-a130-c37f3dc6900a'::uuid, 'drawdown-deploy-offshore-wind-turbines',
     'The recording, the lyrics and credits.',
     'Use only your own words and music or sounds you have the rights to, and don''t film from boats, piers or restricted port areas.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/deploy-offshore-wind-turbines), used with permission; assessment "Deploy Offshore Wind Turbines- Solution Assessment Spreadsheet" by Michael Dioha and Megan Matthews, https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21246039, licensed CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'Offshore wind turbines are ocean-based machines that harness natural wind to generate electricity. These turbines use the relatively strong winds over the water to rotate their blades, which power a generator to make electricity. The electricity travels through underwater cables to reach the land.',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/deploy-offshore-wind-turbines', 'CC BY 4.0', 'https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/', 'https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21246039'),
    ('400c34d6-e2d4-5977-84a6-21373c17f230'::uuid, 'drawdown-deploy-onshore-wind-turbines',
     'A link or screenshot of your submitted or draft comment, with personal contact details hidden.',
     'Use only official comment channels, write honestly in your own words, check the portal''s privacy notice because submitted comments are often published with your name, and don''t visit project sites or private land.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/deploy-onshore-wind-turbines), used with permission; assessment "Deploy Onshore Wind Turbines- Solution Assessment Spreadsheet" by Megan Matthews and Michael Dioha, https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21246129, licensed CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'Onshore wind turbines are land-based machines that harness natural wind to generate electricity. Electricity generation from wind turbines depends on many factors, including natural wind speeds, consistency, and directionality. The Deploy Onshore Wind Turbines solution focuses on utility-scale electricity generation above 1 MW in rated capacity, generally from fields of turbines called wind farms.',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/deploy-onshore-wind-turbines', 'CC BY 4.0', 'https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/', 'https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21246129'),
    ('9890ab86-5e07-5dfc-ab69-40874c388b01'::uuid, 'drawdown-deploy-utility-scale-solar-pv',
     'A screenshot of the map with your notes and source links.',
     'Do this online or view sites only from public roads; don''t enter fenced or private land.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/deploy-utility-scale-solar-pv), used with permission; assessment "Deploy Utility-Scale Solar PV- Solutions Assessment Spreadsheet" by Michael Dioha, Megan Matthews and Al-Amin Bugaje, https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21246284, licensed CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'Utility-scale solar PV refers to large solar power systems, typically installed on open land and connected directly to a central electric grid, that generate electricity for widespread distribution. These systems generally have an installed capacity above 1 MW. There are various configurations of utility-scale solar PV systems and we include fixed-tilt and tracking systems in this solution.',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/deploy-utility-scale-solar-pv', 'CC BY 4.0', 'https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/', 'https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21246284'),
    ('feec02fd-a269-5c00-94ac-c16737ad7546'::uuid, 'drawdown-improve-cement-production',
     'A screenshot of your question and any reply, with names and contact details hidden.',
     'Ask through official public channels, and don''t visit cement plants or construction sites.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/improve-cement-production), used with permission; assessment "Improve Cement Production- Solution Assessment Spreadsheet" by Sarah Gleeson, https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21231071, licensed CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'Cement is a key ingredient of concrete, a manufactured material used in massive quantities around the world. Cement production generates high CO₂ emissions from the production of clinker, a binding ingredient. These emissions come from not only the chemical reaction that produces clinker, but also burning fossil fuels to provide heat for this reaction.',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/improve-cement-production', 'CC BY 4.0', 'https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/', 'https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21231071'),
    ('940ee6f3-0ff8-528c-bc73-30f4a3a03d29'::uuid, 'drawdown-increase-centralized-composting',
     'Your map or list, or a screenshot of your question to the council with names and contact details hidden.',
     'Use official information, follow drop-off rules, and never leave food scraps where they aren''t accepted.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/increase-centralized-composting), used with permission; assessment "Increase Centralized Composting- Solution Assessment Spreadsheet" by Megan Matthews and Sarah Gleeson, https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21246147, licensed CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'A composting system diverts organic waste (OW) from landfills, reducing the production of methane and other GHG emissions. OW is defined as the combination of food waste and green waste, composed of yard and garden trimmings. Composting transforms it into a nutrient-rich soil supplement.',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/increase-centralized-composting', 'CC BY 4.0', 'https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/', 'https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21246147'),
    ('39c075dc-ce16-5321-b1d7-5b75b916a3cb'::uuid, 'drawdown-deploy-industrial-green-hydrogen',
     'Your summary with links to official sources.',
     'Use public records and official meetings only, and don''t visit industrial sites.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/deploy-industrial-green-hydrogen), used with permission; assessment "Deploy Industrial Green Hydrogen- Solution Assessment Spreadsheet" by Heather McDiarmid and Nina F. Farac, https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21246254, licensed CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'In this solution, green hydrogen replaces fossil fuel–based hydrogen for use as a feedstock in the production of more complex molecules such as ammonia for fertilizers and methanol for the production of other commodity chemicals. Green hydrogen production in this solution uses on-site renewable electricity or off-site renewable electricity that directly supplies the facility.',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/deploy-industrial-green-hydrogen', 'CC BY 4.0', 'https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/', 'https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21246254'),
    ('5ce73068-1f93-55dd-a858-c36c2ebeb612'::uuid, 'drawdown-improve-landfill-management',
     'Your summary with source links, or a screenshot of your question with names and contact details hidden.',
     'Research online or ask the agency; never enter landfill grounds.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/improve-landfill-management), used with permission; assessment "Improve Landfill Management- Solution Assessment Spreadsheet" by Jason Lam and Henry Igugu, https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21231060, licensed CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'Landfill management is the process of reducing methane emissions from landfill gas (LFG). As bacteria break down organic waste in an environment without oxygen, they produce methane and release it into the atmosphere if there are no controls in place. This solution focuses on two methane abatement strategies: 1) methane capture/use/destruction and 2) biocovers.',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/improve-landfill-management', 'CC BY 4.0', 'https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/', 'https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21231060'),
    ('34dcd492-e437-500b-8818-fd9dfaa3fbbc'::uuid, 'drawdown-increase-recycling',
     'A photo of the sign posted where you have permission, framed so no names, unit numbers, addresses or people show.',
     'Follow your local official rules, post only where you have permission, and don''t sort through other people''s bins.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/increase-recycling), used with permission; assessment "Increase Recycling- Solution Assessment Spreadsheet" by Nina F. Farac and Megan Matthews, https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21246177, licensed CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'Recycling is a mechanical process that repurposes waste into new products without altering their chemical structure. This solution focuses on four common waste types: metals, paper and cardboard, plastics, and glass. It reduces GHG emissions by minimizing reliance on energy-intensive primary material production, reducing demand for raw materials, and diverting paper from landfills, where decomposition can produce methane.',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/increase-recycling', 'CC BY 4.0', 'https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/', 'https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21246177'),
    ('69a6d95a-447b-5cdc-9d60-064b8dc01d6f'::uuid, 'drawdown-increase-carpooling',
     'A photo of the sign-up sheet or schedule with names, phone numbers and addresses hidden.',
     'Share rides only with people you know or trust and with licensed, insured drivers, make sure everyone wears a seat belt and children ride in the car seats the law requires, let only parents or guardians decide who drives their children, and keep contact details private.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/increase-carpooling), used with permission; assessment "Increase Carpooling- Solution Assessment Spreadsheet" by Heather Jones and Heather McDiarmid, https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21246159, licensed CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'Carpooling entails increasing the occupancy of passenger cars, including taxis, pickup trucks, motorhomes, passenger vans and other such vehicles but not including two- or three-wheeled, freight, public transit, or commercial vehicles, such as buses, heavy trucks, and commercial vans. It replaces the practice of driving alone.',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/increase-carpooling', 'CC BY 4.0', 'https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/', 'https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21246159'),
    ('6b7e9acb-e697-56e8-beb4-417333d2c5db'::uuid, 'drawdown-mobilize-electric-bicycles',
     'A photo or link to your guide with official sources listed.',
     'Quote and link the official rules rather than giving your own legal interpretation, and if you ride, wear a helmet and follow traffic laws.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/mobilize-electric-bicycles), used with permission; assessment "Mobilize Electric Bicycles- Solution Assessment Spreadsheet" by Cameron Roberts and Zoltan Nagy, https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21231092, licensed CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'We define the Mobilize Electric Bicycles solution as increased travel by bicycles that have an electric motor to supplement the effort of the rider, but require the rider to turn the pedals to activate the motor.',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/mobilize-electric-bicycles', 'CC BY 4.0', 'https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/', 'https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21231092'),
    ('febe45f0-f1d6-57ef-a5f4-73ed7e4985c4'::uuid, 'drawdown-mobilize-electric-cars',
     'Your map with the source named.',
     'Use public maps, and if you visit a charger, don''t block it or touch other people''s cars or cables.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/mobilize-electric-cars), used with permission; assessment "Mobilize Electric Cars- Solution Assessment Spreadsheet" by Cameron Roberts and Jason Lam, https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21231076, licensed CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'Electric cars are four-wheeled passenger cars that run on electricity, usually from the electricity grid and stored in onboard batteries (i.e., not including fuel cell electric cars). This definition includes electric pickup trucks, motorhomes, and other such vehicles. It does not include two-wheeled vehicles or hybrid cars (which combine an electric motor with a gasoline or diesel engine).',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/mobilize-electric-cars', 'CC BY 4.0', 'https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/', 'https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21231076'),
    ('0b3adca4-63f1-50aa-a3d8-1fdd8426d787'::uuid, 'drawdown-mobilize-electric-seated-scooters-motorcycles',
     'A short summary of the conversation, with photos only if you had permission.',
     'Ask permission before recording, don''t test-ride anything for this mission, and share names only with consent.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/mobilize-electric-seated-scooters-motorcycles), used with permission; assessment "Mobilize Electric Scooters and Motorcycles- Solution Assessment Spreadsheet" by Heather Jones and Nina F. Farac, https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23375984, licensed CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'Electric scooters and motorcycles are battery-powered two- and three-wheeled vehicles that provide low-emissions mobility. This category of transport includes electric mopeds, motorbikes, seated motor scooters, motorcycles, and three-wheel vehicles, such as e-rickshaws and e-tuk-tuks.',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/mobilize-electric-seated-scooters-motorcycles', 'CC BY 4.0', 'https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/', 'https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23375984'),
    ('e2aa8ccd-9bc3-5941-8e81-3d3cd8cbb57c'::uuid, 'drawdown-mobilize-hybrid-cars',
     'A photo of your chart with the official source named.',
     'Use official ratings, and don''t give anyone buying or financing advice.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/mobilize-hybrid-cars), used with permission; assessment "Mobilize Hybrid Cars- Solution Assessment Spreadsheet" by Heather Jones and Zoltan Nagy, https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.20865760, licensed CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'The Mobilize Hybrid Cars solution entails shifting trips from fossil fuel–powered internal combustion engine (ICE) cars to more efficient, lower emitting hybrid cars. Hybrid cars include hybrid electric cars (HEVs) and plug-in hybrid electric cars (PHEVs). They are four-wheeled passenger cars that combine an ICE with an electric motor and battery to improve fuel efficiency and reduce emissions.',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/mobilize-hybrid-cars', 'CC BY 4.0', 'https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/', 'https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.20865760'),
    ('7fd3053d-e1af-5477-a656-1a38e6569588'::uuid, 'drawdown-improve-nonmotorized-transportation',
     'Your notes and a screenshot of your report with personal details hidden.',
     'Walk in daylight, stay on sidewalks and crossings, note hazards without stepping into traffic, and keep children and other people''s faces out of any photos.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/improve-nonmotorized-transportation), used with permission; assessment "Improve Nonmotorized Transportation- Solution Assessment Spreadsheet" by Cameron Roberts and Heather Jones, https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21231018, licensed CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'We define Improve Nonmotorized Transportation as increasing any form of travel that does not use a motor or engine. In theory, this includes a huge range of transportation modes, including horses, cross-country skis, sailboats, hand-operated rickshaws, and animal-drawn carriages. In practice, pedestrian travel and cycling account for most nonmotorized utilitarian passenger travel.',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/improve-nonmotorized-transportation', 'CC BY 4.0', 'https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/', 'https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21231018'),
    ('a87e5275-c212-51bf-8650-22af893a7fd0'::uuid, 'drawdown-enhance-public-transit',
     'Your notes or photos of the stops and a copy of your feedback message, with your name and contact details hidden.',
     'Visit in daylight, stay on the sidewalk and clear of traffic, and don''t photograph riders'' faces.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/enhance-public-transit), used with permission; assessment "Enhance Public Transit- Solution Assessment Spreadsheet" by Cameron Roberts and Heather Jones, https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21230992, licensed CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'We define the Enhance Public Transit solution as increasing the use of any form of passenger transportation that uses publicly available vehicles (e.g., buses, streetcars, subways, commuter trains, and ferries) operating along fixed routes.',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/enhance-public-transit', 'CC BY 4.0', 'https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/', 'https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21230992'),
    ('8b493fa5-e6c6-5b83-8ac7-83741aa8882d'::uuid, 'drawdown-reduce-crop-residue-burning',
     'A link or photo of your explainer with sources listed.',
     'Research and explain only; never set or go near field fires.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/reduce-crop-residue-burning), used with permission. Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'This solution avoids the burning of crop residues through the adoption of lower-emission options including straw balers, no-till seeders that can plant through residues, and developing markets for residue products. Some promising new techniques are also under development that could further increase future adoption and effectiveness of this solution.',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/reduce-crop-residue-burning', null, null, null),
    ('e86c2226-e09f-59d4-90e6-3a8106cf4c2c'::uuid, 'drawdown-improve-diets',
     'A photo of your dish and recipe card.',
     'Follow basic food safety, list common allergens, and don''t give nutrition or health advice.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/improve-diets), used with permission; assessment "Improve Diets- Solution Assessment Spreadsheet" by Emily Cassidy, https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21246101, licensed CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'We define improved diets as a reduction in ruminant meat consumption and a replacement with other protein-rich foods. Such a diet shift can be adopted incrementally through small behavioral changes that together lead to globally significant reductions in GHG emissions.',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/improve-diets', 'CC BY 4.0', 'https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/', 'https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21246101'),
    ('ed9a7f1a-93f5-5ed7-852e-e99ed689ff36'::uuid, 'drawdown-reduce-food-loss-waste',
     'A photo of your week''s log and the change you picked.',
     'Follow basic food safety, and when in doubt, throw it out rather than eating or sharing questionable food.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/reduce-food-loss-waste), used with permission; assessment "Reduce Food Loss & Waste- Solution Assessment Spreadsheet" by Erika Luna and Aishwarya Venkat, https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21231175, licensed CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'This solution reduces emissions by lowering the amount of food and its associated emissions that are lost or wasted across the supply chain, from production through consumption.',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/reduce-food-loss-waste', 'CC BY 4.0', 'https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/', 'https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21231175'),
    ('6fae6f0d-c160-57ef-9977-3bed661fb77a'::uuid, 'drawdown-improve-nutrient-management',
     'A photo or link to your post or flyer with the official source.',
     'Link to the official rules instead of interpreting them yourself, put up flyers only where you have permission, and don''t handle or spread fertilizer for this mission.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/improve-nutrient-management), used with permission; assessment "Improve Nutrient Management- Solution Assessment Spreadsheet" by Avery Driscoll, https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21230979, licensed CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'We define the Improve Nutrient Management solution as reducing excessive nitrogen use on croplands. Nitrogen is critical for crop production and is added to croplands as synthetic or organic fertilizers and through microbial activity. However, farmers often add more nitrogen to croplands than crops can use.',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/improve-nutrient-management', 'CC BY 4.0', 'https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/', 'https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21230979'),
    ('1321d44c-b8ca-5f2e-975d-a7c1487d5cd0'::uuid, 'drawdown-improve-rice-production',
     'A link or photo of your explainer with sources listed.',
     'Stick to reliable sources, and don''t claim results your sources don''t support.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/improve-rice-production), used with permission; assessment "Improve Rice Production- Solution Assessment Spreadsheet" by Eric Toensmeier and Zoltan Nagy, https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21246058, licensed CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'Rice production is a significant source of methane emissions and a minor source of nitrous oxide emissions. Most rice production occurs in flooded fields called paddies, where anaerobic conditions trigger high levels of methane production. This solution includes two related practices that each reduce emissions from paddy rice production: noncontinuous flooding and nutrient management.',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/improve-rice-production', 'CC BY 4.0', 'https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/', 'https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21246058'),
    ('31490c0d-4a7a-5e86-a3a7-9904e1b872ad'::uuid, 'drawdown-improve-annual-cropping',
     'A photo or link to your guide with sources listed.',
     'Base it on reliable local sources, and plant only on land where you have permission.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/improve-annual-cropping), used with permission; assessment "Improve Annual Cropping- Solution Assessment Spreadsheet" by Eric Toensme and Zoltan Nagy, https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21246076, licensed CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'Project Drawdown’s Improve Annual Cropping solution is a set of practices that protects soils by minimizing plowing (no-till/reduced tillage) and maintaining continuous soil cover (by retaining crop residues or growing cover crops). This increases soil carbon sequestration and reduces nitrous oxide emissions.',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/improve-annual-cropping', 'CC BY 4.0', 'https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/', 'https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21246076'),
    ('5a898376-c3f7-57b3-9029-be155f809f2f'::uuid, 'drawdown-protect-coastal-wetlands',
     'Your map with links to the sources.',
     'Use public maps, and if you visit, check tide times, stay on boardwalks and don''t walk on marsh plants or seagrass.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/protect-coastal-wetlands), used with permission; assessment "Protect Coastal Wetlands- Solution Assessment Spreadsheet" by Christina Richardson and Avery Driscoll, https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21246009, licensed CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'Coastal wetland protection is the long-term protection of mangrove, salt marsh, and seagrass ecosystems from degradation by human activities. This solution focuses on legal mechanisms of coastal wetland protection, including the establishment of Protected Areas (PAs) and Marine Protected Areas (MPAs), which are managed with the primary goal of conserving nature.',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/protect-coastal-wetlands', 'CC BY 4.0', 'https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/', 'https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21246009'),
    ('e459b18c-7352-5f7c-b93c-d5cb383f850c'::uuid, 'drawdown-protect-forests',
     'Your summary with links to the maps and agency pages.',
     'Research online, and if you visit, stay on marked trails and follow posted rules.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/protect-forests), used with permission; assessment "Protect Forests- Solution Assessment Spreadsheet" by Avery Driscoll and Megan Matthews, https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21230935, licensed CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'We define the Protect Forests solution as the long-term protection of tree-dominated ecosystems through establishment of protected areas (PAs), managed with the primary goal of conserving nature, and land tenure for Indigenous peoples. These protections reduce forest degradation, avoiding GHG emissions and ensuring continued carbon sequestration by healthy forests. This solution addresses protection of forests on mineral soils.',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/protect-forests', 'CC BY 4.0', 'https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/', 'https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21230935'),
    ('b2a88b65-1e5b-5da4-9af7-011ca8f7874f'::uuid, 'drawdown-protect-grasslands-savannas',
     'Your map with links to the sources.',
     'Research online, and if you visit, stay on marked trails and follow posted rules.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/protect-grasslands-savannas), used with permission; assessment "Protect Grasslands and Savannas- Solution Assessment Spreadsheet" by Avery Driscoll and Christina Richardson, https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21246118, licensed CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'This solution focuses on the legal protection of grassland and savanna ecosystems through the establishment of protected areas (PAs), which are managed with the primary goal of conserving nature, and land tenure for Indigenous peoples. These protections reduce grassland degradation, which preserves carbon stored in soils and vegetation and enables continued carbon sequestration by healthy grasslands.',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/protect-grasslands-savannas', 'CC BY 4.0', 'https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/', 'https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21246118'),
    ('f0533986-f7c6-53bd-82b4-c311e9875cb3'::uuid, 'drawdown-protect-peatlands',
     'A photo of your notes or a list of the products you checked.',
     'Read labels without opening bags, and don''t tell anyone which brand they must buy.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/protect-peatlands), used with permission; assessment "Protect Peatlands- Solution Assessment Spreadsheet" by Avery Driscoll and Megan Matthews, https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21245970, licensed CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'The Protect Peatlands solution is defined as legally protecting peatland ecosystems through establishment of protected areas (PAs), which preserves stored carbon and ensures continued carbon sequestration by reducing degradation of the natural hydrology, soils, and/or vegetation. This solution focuses on non-coastal peatlands that have not yet been drained or otherwise severely degraded.',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/protect-peatlands', 'CC BY 4.0', 'https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/', 'https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21245970'),
    ('960f0604-0a15-5012-aef8-a70418b535e3'::uuid, 'drawdown-protect-seaweed-ecosystems',
     'A link to your video, slideshow or comic with sources.',
     'Use your own footage or clips you have permission to use, and don''t harvest seaweed or dive for this mission.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/protect-seaweed-ecosystems), used with permission; assessment "Protect Seaweed Ecosystems- Solution Assessment Spreadsheet" by Christina Richardson and Avery Driscoll, https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21245985, licensed CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'Seaweed ecosystem protection is the long-term protection from degradation of wild subtidal brown and red seaweed ecosystems. Seaweeds, also called macroalgae, are photosynthetic marine organisms that absorb CO₂ from the water and convert it into biomass. This can lower surface-water CO₂ concentrations, allowing additional CO₂ from the atmosphere to be dissolved in the ocean.',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/protect-seaweed-ecosystems', 'CC BY 4.0', 'https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/', 'https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21245985'),
    ('216568f0-243f-5cac-91b9-4b4ae8b571ed'::uuid, 'drawdown-restore-forests',
     'A photo of your work, with no one else''s face unless they agreed, or a link to where you shared the event.',
     'Plant only with an organized group that has the landowner''s permission, wear gloves and sturdy shoes, and follow the leaders'' safety briefing.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/restore-forests), used with permission; assessment "Restore Forests- Solution Assessment Spreadsheet" by Avery Driscoll and Megan Matthews, https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22002754, licensed CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'Forest restoration is the process of returning previously forested land to a forested state. As forests regrow, they remove carbon from the atmosphere and sequester it in biomass.',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/restore-forests', 'CC BY 4.0', 'https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/', 'https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22002754'),
    ('5b79bc68-40a5-5a3a-835f-23ab6b83e99e'::uuid, 'drawdown-restore-peatlands',
     'Your summary with links to the project.',
     'Bogs can be dangerous to walk on, so if you visit, stay on boardwalks and marked paths at public sites.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/restore-peatlands), used with permission; assessment "Restore Peatlands- Solution Assessment Spreadsheet" by Avery Driscoll and Christina Richardson, https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23377700, licensed CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'Peatland restoration is the process of returning peat-forming vegetation and natural hydrologic conditions to degraded peatlands. Restoration of peatlands stops GHG emissions from peat degradation and removes carbon through sequestration in biomass and peat.',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/restore-peatlands', 'CC BY 4.0', 'https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/', 'https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23377700'),
    ('1c2eaace-0753-5afa-b538-dc8989ed529e'::uuid, 'drawdown-deploy-silvopasture',
     'A photo of your labeled drawing or painting.',
     'Use your own artwork, and if you visit a farm, go only with the farmer''s invitation and keep away from livestock.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/deploy-silvopasture), used with permission; assessment "Deploy Silvopasture- Solution Assessment Spreadsheet" by Eric Toensmeier, https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21246087, licensed CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'We define the Deploy Silvopasture solution as the adoption of agroforestry practices that add trees to grazing land, including planted pastures and natural rangelands. (Note that this solution does NOT include creating forested grazing land by thinning existing forest; this is a form of deforestation and not desirable in terms of climate.)',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/deploy-silvopasture', 'CC BY 4.0', 'https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/', 'https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21246087'),
    ('60df48e0-d185-5852-99ae-7bf2a245e853'::uuid, 'drawdown-use-biochar',
     'A short summary of the conversation, without names unless people agreed.',
     'Don''t try to make biochar yourself, since it involves fire; just ask and share what you learn.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/use-biochar), used with permission; assessment "Use Biochar- Solution Assessment Spreadsheet" by Jason Lam and Megan Matthews, https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23377743, licensed CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'Producing biochar is the process of taking organic matter such as crop residues, animal manure, and forest residues and converting it into a charcoal-like substance known as biochar. Producing biochar removes carbon from the atmosphere by transforming carbon absorbed by plants and animals into a highly stable form, preventing it from quickly returning to the atmosphere (Belmont & Sanchez, 2025).',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/use-biochar', 'CC BY 4.0', 'https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/', 'https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23377743'),
    ('3a9da222-581a-51ec-b5ae-a2599c35f46d'::uuid, 'drawdown-boost-appliance-equipment-efficiency',
     'A link or photo of your explainer.',
     'Explain what the label shows and link to the official guide, without telling anyone which product to buy.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/boost-appliance-equipment-efficiency), used with permission. Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'Boosting the efficiency of appliances and equipment cuts GHG emissions by reducing the amount of electricity used to operate these devices. Efficiency improvements also lead to reduced peak demand, less strain on the electric grid, and potential utility savings for homeowners due to reduced electricity use.',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/boost-appliance-equipment-efficiency', null, null, null),
    ('ff5325cd-8f20-5ccf-9949-089b806a1d54'::uuid, 'drawdown-improve-building-envelopes',
     'A photo or link to your list in the place you shared it.',
     'Link only to official program pages, post only where you have permission, don''t promise anyone they will qualify, and don''t give financial advice.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/improve-building-envelopes), used with permission; assessment "Improve Building Envelopes- Solution Assessment Spreadsheet" by Henry Igugu and Nina F. Farac, https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23377578, licensed CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'Improve Building Envelopes cuts GHG emissions by enhancing the thermal resistance of the building shell, reducing unwanted heat exchange between the external environment and indoor spaces. These thermal improvements help decrease the amount of energy required to heat and cool buildings and the associated emissions.',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/improve-building-envelopes', 'CC BY 4.0', 'https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/', 'https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23377578'),
    ('1b0ab594-ac54-5909-a768-a35e518a1449'::uuid, 'drawdown-deploy-green-roofs',
     'Your summary with source links, or a screenshot of the question you sent, with names and contact details hidden.',
     'Use public sources and official contact channels, and don''t go onto any rooftops.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/deploy-green-roofs), used with permission. Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'Green roofs sequester carbon through photosynthesis and may reduce energy consumption and emissions from cooling and heating the building thanks to the added insulation and the cooling effects of plants (Getter et al., 2009; He et al., 2023).',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/deploy-green-roofs', null, null, null),
    ('f7eeae72-b28f-5183-a392-f527edaf73ec'::uuid, 'drawdown-use-low-flow-fixtures',
     'A photo of your timing notes and a link to any local water-saving offer.',
     'Use cold water to avoid scalds, mop up spills so no one slips, and don''t take fixtures apart.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/use-low-flow-fixtures), used with permission. Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'Low-flow fixtures reduce GHG emissions by reducing the volume of hot water used and therefore reducing the emissions from the energy used to heat that water (Kenway et al., 2023). Reduced water usage also leads to fewer emissions from treating and pumping water for domestic use (Yateh et al., 2024). Low-flow fixtures are low-cost and simple to install.',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/use-low-flow-fixtures', null, null, null),
    ('9d1fdc5d-7617-5408-9269-8937cde77c7a'::uuid, 'drawdown-deploy-cool-roofs',
     'A screenshot or photo of your marked-up map or tally.',
     'Do this from online maps only; don''t go onto roofs or private property, leave your own home unmarked, and don''t single out individual homes or homeowners.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/deploy-cool-roofs), used with permission. Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'Cool roofs cut GHG emissions from electricity generation by lowering the amount of cooling required to condition indoor spaces, thereby decreasing the use of air conditioners. Using cool roofs in building design lowers electricity use, improves thermal comfort for building occupants, and is relatively cheap to deploy.',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/deploy-cool-roofs', null, null, null),
    ('a6793da7-d182-5fa1-bf42-59bbc9796347'::uuid, 'drawdown-increase-decentralized-composting',
     'A photo of your work, with no one else''s face unless they agreed, or a short note on what you learned.',
     'Join an organized session, wear gloves and closed shoes, follow the site''s rules, and wash your hands afterward.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/increase-decentralized-composting), used with permission. Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'Decentralized composting systems involve waste generators in converting organic waste (OW) into a nutrient-rich soil supplement. They include a broad range of composting scales, from single households and community gardens to commercial and institutional operations (Platt, 2017).',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/increase-decentralized-composting', null, null, null),
    ('56b4c743-10a0-5148-ae60-323c3e0d1564'::uuid, 'drawdown-improve-fishing-vessel-efficiency',
     'A short summary of the conversation, with a photo only if you had permission.',
     'Ask politely, accept no for an answer, and share names or photos only with permission.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/improve-fishing-vessel-efficiency), used with permission. Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'Improving fishing vessel efficiency cuts CO₂ emissions in wild capture fisheries by lowering fuel use through vessel, gear, or operational modifications. Advantages include the long-term cost savings from fuel use reductions, the ability to implement many of these improvements without reducing fishing effort, and the potential additional benefits for air quality and marine ecosystems.',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/improve-fishing-vessel-efficiency', null, null, null),
    ('cdc236e3-e4bd-5323-bcd4-ee9c4d77f135'::uuid, 'drawdown-improve-aquaculture',
     'A photo of your chart and the source for the label you looked up.',
     'Read labels without handling products unnecessarily, and ask staff politely if you have questions.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/improve-aquaculture), used with permission. Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'Improving aquaculture involves reducing CO₂ and other GHG emissions during the production of farmed fish and other aquatic animals through better feed efficiency and the decarbonization of on-farm energy use. Advantages include reduced demand for feedstocks produced from both wild capture fisheries and terrestrial sources, which benefits marine and terrestrial ecosystems.',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/improve-aquaculture', null, null, null),
    ('da0a9a12-65d1-5a46-bcce-f359ebf13333'::uuid, 'drawdown-deploy-electric-irrigation-pumps',
     'A link or photo of your explainer with sources listed.',
     'Research and explain only; don''t touch or operate pumps, wells or electrical equipment.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/deploy-electric-irrigation-pumps), used with permission. Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'Replacing fossil-fuel-powered irrigation pumps with electric pumps powered by the grid can reduce emissions in most regions of the world. Electric irrigation pumps, which can also be powered by on-site clean energy, are more efficient than fossil fuel pumps. They are already cost-competitive and widely used, and adoption is increasing.',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/deploy-electric-irrigation-pumps', null, null, null),
    ('fabf57f7-bd14-5ec5-a980-41397329157a'::uuid, 'drawdown-improve-manure-management',
     'Your summary with links to the agency''s rules or records, with no farm owners'' names or home addresses.',
     'Use public records only, don''t name farm owners or post their addresses, and never enter farms or go near manure storage, which can release deadly gases.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/improve-manure-management), used with permission. Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'Improved manure management refers to the use of impermeable covers and physical or chemical treatments applied during the storage and processing of wet manure. These techniques can reduce methane emissions under anaerobic storage conditions and nitrous oxide emissions under aerobic conditions.',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/improve-manure-management', null, null, null),
    ('38f5c62c-a8cb-5ac4-b0b1-aba602a400d5'::uuid, 'drawdown-reduce-overfishing',
     'Your summary with links to the agency reports.',
     'Use official fisheries sources, and if you fish, follow local licenses and limits.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/reduce-overfishing), used with permission. Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'Reduce Overfishing refers to the use of management actions that decrease fishing effort and therefore cut CO₂ emissions from fishing vessel fuel use on overfished stocks. Advantages include the potential to replenish depleted fish stocks, support ecosystem health, and enhance long-term food and job security.',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/reduce-overfishing', null, null, null),
    ('b5a1b342-9b1c-537e-920b-98226ad45669'::uuid, 'drawdown-protect-seafloors',
     'Your map or table with links to the sources.',
     'Research online, and if you visit the coast, stay in public areas and watch the tide.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/protect-seafloors), used with permission. Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'Protect Seafloors is the long-term protection of the seafloor from degradation, which helps preserve existing sediment carbon stocks and avoid CO₂ emissions. Advantages of seafloor protection include the conservation of biodiversity and marine ecosystems, potentially low costs, and the ability for immediate implementation.',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/protect-seafloors', null, null, null),
    ('dfb7d2eb-1373-59ae-bacd-22668b604f68'::uuid, 'drawdown-restore-grasslands-savannas',
     'A photo of your identification card with sources listed.',
     'Photograph or draw plants instead of picking them, stay on trails, don''t touch plants you can''t identify, since some cause rashes or burns, and wash your hands afterward.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/restore-grasslands-savannas), used with permission. Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'Grassland and savanna restoration removes CO₂ from the atmosphere through photosynthesis as the ecosystem regrows, storing carbon in soils and vegetation. Grassland and savanna restoration faces relatively low barriers to implementation, provides substantial benefits for biodiversity, and may be deployable on large land areas.',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/restore-grasslands-savannas', null, null, null),
    ('74a7935a-731f-5f35-ad12-f1799e22d378'::uuid, 'drawdown-restore-mangrove-ecosystems',
     'A photo of your labeled artwork.',
     'Use your own artwork, and if you visit mangroves, stay on public boardwalks and watch the tides.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/restore-mangrove-ecosystems), used with permission. Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'Restore Mangrove Ecosystems removes carbon by re-establishing mangrove forests in areas where they were previously destroyed by conversion or other disturbances. This allows carbon to accumulate in above- and below-ground biomass and sediment. Advantages include mangrove forests'' high effectiveness at carbon removal and storage, as well as their numerous environmental benefits and generally low cost.',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/restore-mangrove-ecosystems', null, null, null),
    ('96685219-f741-5c38-97ad-cdc5eceba121'::uuid, 'drawdown-restore-salt-marsh-ecosystems',
     'A photo of your work, with no one else''s face unless they agreed, or a link to where you shared the project.',
     'Join only organized groups and follow the leaders'' safety briefing, wear gloves and sturdy shoes, check the tide and stay out of the water, leave sharp or hazardous items for the organizers, and stay off fragile marsh plants.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/restore-salt-marsh-ecosystems), used with permission. Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'Restore Salt Marsh Ecosystems involves actively reestablishing salt marshes in areas where they were previously lost to conversion or other disturbance, allowing vegetation to regrow and carbon to accumulate in biomass and sediments. Advantages include salt marshes’ ability to durably store substantial quantities of carbon over long time periods and their numerous co-benefits for the environment and humans.',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/restore-salt-marsh-ecosystems', null, null, null),
    ('78ab0a5d-ca2b-52b2-a9d0-54827b5f3fd7'::uuid, 'drawdown-restore-seagrass-ecosystems',
     'A photo of your card and where you shared it.',
     'Base it on official guidance, and post or hand it out only where you have permission.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/restore-seagrass-ecosystems), used with permission. Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'Restore Seagrass Ecosystems involves reestablishing seagrass meadows in ocean areas where they were lost due to disturbances or degradation. As seagrasses grow, they remove CO₂ from ocean water through photosynthesis and accumulate carbon in their biomass, which allows seawater to take up additional CO₂ from the atmosphere.',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/restore-seagrass-ecosystems', null, null, null),
    ('a4f79ed1-4534-57fc-a181-33e95fc87b0c'::uuid, 'drawdown-restore-seaweed-ecosystems',
     'Your summary with links to the project.',
     'Follow along online, and join any in-water activity only through the project''s official volunteer program.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/restore-seaweed-ecosystems), used with permission. Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'Seaweed (also called macroalgae) ecosystem restoration involves the reestablishment of wild red, brown, and green seaweed through interventions that recover degraded, damaged, or destroyed seaweed ecosystems. Healthy seaweed ecosystems remove CO₂ from the water column and convert it into biomass through photosynthesis, allowing additional CO₂ to be taken up in the ocean from the atmosphere.',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/restore-seaweed-ecosystems', null, null, null),
    ('ff2a6de8-b97e-5642-acb6-25b39fcc4a9a'::uuid, 'drawdown-improve-fuel-burning-cooking-equipment',
     'A link or photo of your explainer with sources named.',
     'Share information from recognized sources without giving medical advice, and don''t test stoves or burn anything indoors.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/improve-fuel-burning-cooking-equipment), used with permission. Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'In low- and middle-income countries, adopting cooking equipment that uses cleaner fuels or is more efficient has the potential to reduce GHG emissions from both cooking and deforestation due to unsustainable biomass use. Such equipment is readily available and inexpensive and provides significant social benefits. Barriers to adoption include cost and cultural practices, particularly in sub-Saharan Africa.',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/improve-fuel-burning-cooking-equipment', null, null, null),
    ('4f17538c-53b5-5c0e-9a9a-2d8ff007990f'::uuid, 'drawdown-deploy-electric-cooking-equipment',
     'A photo of your dish and recipe card.',
     'Follow the appliance instructions, don''t use damaged cords or overloaded outlets, and follow basic food safety.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/deploy-electric-cooking-equipment), used with permission. Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'Electric cooking equipment such as electric resistance stoves, induction stoves, and electric ovens can replace fuel-burning cooking equipment and reduce cooking-related GHG emissions, especially in regions with low-emission electricity grids. Cooking with electricity has significant health, safety, and energy efficiency benefits but cost, reliable access to electricity, and cultural compatibility are barriers to adoption.',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/deploy-electric-cooking-equipment', null, null, null),
    ('9991a89f-e662-599f-84d2-e13c725e139d'::uuid, 'drawdown-deploy-district-cooling',
     'A photo of your diagram or comic with sources listed.',
     'Work from public sources and don''t visit plants or restricted utility areas.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/deploy-district-cooling), used with permission. Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'Deploying district cooling is the process of connecting multiple buildings in a dense area to a single, highly efficient source of cooling. The increased energy efficiency and reduction in use of high global warming potential refrigerants can translate into substantial emissions reductions and lower operating expenses (International Energy Agency [IEA], 2018; Energy Sector Management Assistance Program, 2020).',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/deploy-district-cooling', null, null, null),
    ('728a63c6-8282-5cf3-91c6-90578935883d'::uuid, 'drawdown-deploy-micro-wind-turbines',
     'A photo of your diary pages or chart.',
     'Observe from the ground or indoors; stay off roofs and away from power lines.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/deploy-micro-wind-turbines), used with permission. Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'Micro wind turbines harness natural wind to generate electricity. They can operate independently or be connected to a centralized electricity grid, and are useful for small-scale commercial, agricultural, and residential applications. Advantages include reducing reliance on fossil fuels for electricity generation, potential expansion of electrification to rural areas, and improvement in energy equity and independence worldwide.',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/deploy-micro-wind-turbines', null, null, null),
    ('1bd34e77-5d56-532f-8989-77f1bde20630'::uuid, 'drawdown-deploy-nuclear-fusion',
     'A link or photo of your explainer with sources listed.',
     'Stick to reputable sources and avoid hype or scary claims you can''t back up.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/deploy-nuclear-fusion), used with permission. Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'Nuclear fusion combines two elements in a nuclear reaction to form a larger element and release energy that can be used to generate electricity. Nuclear fusion has been researched since the 1950s, but there have been no nuclear fusion plants built to date.',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/deploy-nuclear-fusion', null, null, null),
    ('9f545890-788e-5ce4-b6ce-042251b8d441'::uuid, 'drawdown-deploy-small-modular-nuclear-reactors',
     'Your summary with links to the regulator''s records.',
     'Use the regulator''s public records and public meetings only, and don''t approach nuclear or industrial sites.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/deploy-small-modular-nuclear-reactors), used with permission. Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'Small modular nuclear reactors (SMRs) are advanced reactors designed to produce low-carbon electricity using smaller units that are factory-fabricated. SMRs aim to overcome the safety, cost, and scalability challenges of traditional large-scale nuclear power. They offer benefits such as passive safety systems, lower capital investment, and the potential to be deployed flexibly in remote or underserved regions.',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/deploy-small-modular-nuclear-reactors', null, null, null),
    ('f364102d-e11f-583a-8249-e8ce07615a75'::uuid, 'drawdown-deploy-advanced-geothermal-energy',
     'A link to your video, slideshow or comic with sources listed.',
     'Stick to reputable sources, and don''t visit drilling or plant sites.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/deploy-advanced-geothermal-energy), used with permission. Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'Advanced geothermal energy is an emerging clean energy technology that harnesses the Earth’s subsurface heat to generate emissions-free baseload and dispatchable electricity and heat.',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/deploy-advanced-geothermal-energy', null, null, null),
    ('1ba35152-acfa-5786-8eb7-015bfa01c232'::uuid, 'drawdown-deploy-methane-digesters',
     'A short summary with links, or a screenshot of your question and any reply, with names and contact details hidden.',
     'Use public information or official tours only, and never enter treatment plant grounds or go near tanks on your own.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/deploy-methane-digesters), used with permission. Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'Methane digesters are specialized devices that use anaerobic digestion to convert agricultural, industrial, or municipal organic waste into biogas and digestate, a nutrient-rich material. Treating organic waste using a methane digester reduces emissions by capturing methane that would have been released during uncontrolled anaerobic decomposition in a landfill or manure lagoon.',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/deploy-methane-digesters', null, null, null),
    ('3fb16043-b210-577e-b662-670cb9df0296'::uuid, 'drawdown-improve-district-heating-industry',
     'A screenshot of your question and any reply, with names and contact details hidden, plus links to the plans you checked.',
     'Use official channels and public documents, and don''t visit industrial sites.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/improve-district-heating-industry), used with permission. Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'Improving district heating for industry involves using low-carbon alternatives, such as electric boilers, heat pumps, and waste heat from other industries, to provide heat to industries for their operations. Currently, most district heating for industry relies heavily on fossil fuels to generate heat (International Energy Agency [IEA], 2026).',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/improve-district-heating-industry', null, null, null),
    ('29222f7a-28ca-54ba-970f-bbef5c525b0f'::uuid, 'drawdown-deploy-plastic-alternatives-bioplastics',
     'A photo or link to your post or sign with the official source named.',
     'Use the official local guidance, put up signs only where you have permission, and don''t sort through anyone else''s bins.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/deploy-plastic-alternatives-bioplastics), used with permission. Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'Bioplastics are renewable, plant-based alternatives to conventional plastics that can reduce emissions by replacing fossil-based feedstocks with biogenic carbon feedstocks. These feedstocks are biomass materials that absorb atmospheric CO₂ during growth and serve as the carbon source for plastic production.',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/deploy-plastic-alternatives-bioplastics', null, null, null),
    ('940d2140-eb2f-58dc-b798-4ffc96fff671'::uuid, 'drawdown-improve-steel-production',
     'A photo or link to your timeline with sources listed.',
     'Research only; don''t visit mills, scrapyards or industrial sites.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/improve-steel-production), used with permission. Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'Improve Steel Production involves replacing the use of fossil fuels in making steel from iron ore with electrolytic hydrogen and clean electricity.',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/improve-steel-production', null, null, null),
    ('154bc628-8758-51ed-924a-1dd61ed2e171'::uuid, 'drawdown-reduce-airplane-contrails',
     'A photo of your sky diary or sky photos with your notes.',
     'Never look at the sun or point a camera straight at it, and watch from a safe place on the ground.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/reduce-airplane-contrails), used with permission. Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'Contrails, the long, thin clouds that form behind airplanes, trap heat radiating from the Earth, creating a strong but short-lived warming effect similar to that of GHGs in the atmosphere (Kärcher, 2018; Thomas et al., 2025). Rerouting airplanes to avoid areas where warming contrails can form reduces the warming impact of these human-made clouds (Martin Frias et al., 2024).',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/reduce-airplane-contrails', null, null, null),
    ('4a35883c-a97e-5422-bd31-c5a6e4763554'::uuid, 'drawdown-mobilize-green-hydrogen-for-aviation-and-trucking',
     'A photo or link to your chart with sources listed.',
     'Present both sides fairly, and don''t handle fuels or gas containers.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/mobilize-green-hydrogen-for-aviation-and-trucking), used with permission. Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'Green hydrogen is an emissions-free fuel produced by using renewable electricity to split water into hydrogen and oxygen. For aviation and long-haul trucking, green hydrogen can be used either directly in fuel cells or combusted in modified engines, offering a potential pathway to deep emissions reductions.',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/mobilize-green-hydrogen-for-aviation-and-trucking', null, null, null),
    ('12db7169-9d11-5a35-988c-d58c8d0a3c86'::uuid, 'drawdown-deploy-sustainable-aviation-fuel',
     'Your summary with links to the airline statement and the independent sources.',
     'Quote sources accurately, stick to what they say, and don''t accuse anyone of wrongdoing.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/deploy-sustainable-aviation-fuel), used with permission. Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'Sustainable aviation fuel (SAF) is a low-carbon alternative to conventional jet fuel. It is made from renewable feedstocks, including waste oils, agricultural residues, and renewable electricity. However, when combustion emissions are considered, SAF does not consistently reduce emissions when compared to conventional fuels. SAF is already in use in commercial flights at low blending levels.',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/deploy-sustainable-aviation-fuel', null, null, null),
    ('0f2c4e86-82a9-5e77-9998-68ddb3c337fa'::uuid, 'drawdown-advance-cultivated-meat',
     'A short, anonymous summary of the answers you gathered.',
     'Ask only willing people, keep answers anonymous, and don''t pressure anyone.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/advance-cultivated-meat), used with permission. Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'Cultivated meat is produced from a sample of animal cells, rather than by slaughtering animals. This technology shows promise for reducing emissions from animal agriculture, but its climate impact depends on the energy source used during production.',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/advance-cultivated-meat', null, null, null),
    ('22458ffa-9f2e-5a40-b72f-921a3a09b5a0'::uuid, 'drawdown-use-feed-additives',
     'A link to your video, comic or post with sources listed.',
     'Don''t give advice on feeding animals, and stick to what reliable sources say.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/use-feed-additives), used with permission. Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'Feed additives can reduce enteric methane production in ruminant livestock, such as cattle, goats, and sheep. Most feed additive compounds are still being researched to determine their efficacy and safety; however, at least one product, 3-NOP (3-nitrooxypropanol), has been shown to be effective, has recently been approved for use in many countries, and has experienced some early adoption.',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/use-feed-additives', null, null, null),
    ('a67c7c74-c7f6-55fc-b546-3ea4b959745a'::uuid, 'drawdown-improve-irrigation-water-use-efficiency',
     'A photo of your rain jar and your week of notes.',
     'Keep the jar on the ground rather than on a roof or ledge, and empty it after each reading so mosquitoes can''t breed.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/improve-irrigation-water-use-efficiency), used with permission. Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'Irrigation water use efficiency involves reducing water use without compromising crop productivity by improving irrigation scheduling and/or equipment. Irrigation produces GHG emissions by altering biogeochemical cycling of carbon and nitrogen cycles in water and soils, and through energy use for pumping.',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/improve-irrigation-water-use-efficiency', null, null, null),
    ('f9085849-2b32-5436-8bbe-99e52ed4e57b'::uuid, 'drawdown-deploy-leaf-protein-concentrates',
     'A photo or link to your fact sheet with sources listed.',
     'Research and explain only; don''t forage, process or eat wild plants, and don''t give nutrition advice.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/deploy-leaf-protein-concentrates), used with permission. Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'Deploying leaf protein concentrates (LPCs) involves isolating high-quality proteins from green foliage, agricultural by-products, or aquatic flora for use in human food and animal feed.',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/deploy-leaf-protein-concentrates', null, null, null),
    ('f3e231f6-139d-504b-952e-b7deb39f9422'::uuid, 'drawdown-improve-ruminant-breeding',
     'Your summary with a link to the talk.',
     'Use free public talks or university pages, and don''t visit farms without an invitation.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/improve-ruminant-breeding), used with permission. Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'Ruminant livestock, such as cattle, goats, and sheep, can be selectively bred for reduced enteric methane production.',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/improve-ruminant-breeding', null, null, null),
    ('ffc85842-a7a4-5629-a9c1-8b41a58eb5c1'::uuid, 'drawdown-deploy-seaweed-farming-for-food',
     'A photo of your dish and the recipe with your source.',
     'Buy seaweed sold as food rather than collecting it, and check allergies and dietary limits before sharing.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/deploy-seaweed-farming-for-food), used with permission. Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'Deploy Seaweed Farming for Food involves cultivating seaweed (often called macroalgae) in the ocean for human consumption as a partial replacement for low-protein foods grown on land (e.g., grains, vegetables). This solution considers the emissions avoided by substituting one kilogram of low-protein food with one kilogram of seaweed.',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/deploy-seaweed-farming-for-food', null, null, null),
    ('93e0f0e8-0fe4-59f7-907f-05ac7287a250'::uuid, 'drawdown-deploy-alternative-grazing',
     'Your summary with links to any published guides, or a summary of the reply you received, without the advisor''s name or contact details.',
     'Ask through official channels, and don''t visit farms or approach livestock without an invitation.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/deploy-alternative-grazing), used with permission. Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'Alternative grazing refers to approaches to managing ruminant livestock – including multiple fenced paddocks and frequent animal movement, short grazing periods, and enforced rest periods for forage – that aim to increase soil organic carbon (SOC) by allowing vegetation to recover.',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/deploy-alternative-grazing', null, null, null),
    ('1a9c8fcb-2a76-56de-b019-9c1f23a19800'::uuid, 'drawdown-deploy-enhanced-rock-weathering',
     'A link or photo of your explainer with sources listed.',
     'Research and explain only; don''t spread rock dust or run field experiments.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/deploy-enhanced-rock-weathering), used with permission. Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'Enhanced rock weathering removes CO₂ from the air by accelerating the natural chemical and physical breakdown of certain rocks. This carbon removal practice can be effective and has been deployed in pilot and small-scale commercial projects.',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/deploy-enhanced-rock-weathering', null, null, null),
    ('2bab59bf-f317-5962-bdaa-2ee1ebbb664a'::uuid, 'drawdown-reduce-grazing-intensity',
     'A link or photo of your explainer with sources listed.',
     'Stick to reliable sources, and if you visit grazing land, stay on public trails and away from livestock.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/reduce-grazing-intensity), used with permission. Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'Reducing grazing intensity involves lowering ruminant livestock stocking rates or grazing pressure. This removes carbon from the atmosphere by reducing land damage and increasing soil organic carbon (SOC).',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/reduce-grazing-intensity', null, null, null),
    ('3f646f9c-5619-54ed-b38a-3977d359c61c'::uuid, 'drawdown-restore-large-herbivores',
     'A photo or link to your poster or post with sources listed.',
     'Research only, and never approach, feed or follow wild animals.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/restore-large-herbivores), used with permission. Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'Reintroducing or increasing the populations of large wild herbivores – such as bison, elephants, and moose – in natural and degraded ecosystems alters habitats, potentially leading to greater carbon removal from the atmosphere and increased carbon storage in vegetation and soils. However, evidence of its effectiveness is limited and mixed.',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/restore-large-herbivores', null, null, null),
    ('3933adb5-41e2-57fc-9f40-a2cf8f7ab0f4'::uuid, 'drawdown-deploy-ocean-alkalinity-enhancement',
     'Your explainer with sources listed.',
     'Present more than one view fairly, and don''t run experiments with seawater or minerals.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/deploy-ocean-alkalinity-enhancement), used with permission. Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'Ocean alkalinity enhancement (OAE) increases the ocean’s natural ability to remove CO₂ from the air by increasing the alkalinity of ocean water. This carbon removal practice could be globally effective at removing CO₂ at the gigaton level annually and is currently being tested in field studies.',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/deploy-ocean-alkalinity-enhancement', null, null, null),
    ('9f0aea98-532e-5160-8e48-eb1f76dcea68'::uuid, 'drawdown-deploy-ocean-electrochemistry',
     'Your list of questions and answers with sources.',
     'Research only; don''t try electrical experiments with water.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/deploy-ocean-electrochemistry), used with permission. Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'Deploy Ocean Electrochemistry uses electricity to separate seawater into acidic and basic solutions, which can be used to remove CO₂ in different ways. Acidic streams can be used to alter the chemistry of seawater, either by releasing dissolved CO₂ for capture and long-term storage or by weathering alkaline rocks and increasing seawater alkalinity.',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/deploy-ocean-electrochemistry', null, null, null),
    ('747455c5-6ce7-5aa0-9363-e3dd41f8e954'::uuid, 'drawdown-restore-whale-populations',
     'Your story with sources listed.',
     'Use reliable sources, and if you go whale watching, follow official viewing rules and distances.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/restore-whale-populations), used with permission. Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'Whales play a critical role in the ocean carbon cycle, but commercial whaling in the 20th century drastically diminished their populations. Restoring the abundance of whales to pre-whaling levels has been proposed as a way to remove additional CO₂ from the atmosphere and store it in the ocean.',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/restore-whale-populations', null, null, null),
    ('91846487-707c-509d-b421-488fcd896853'::uuid, 'drawdown-bury-biomass',
     'Your summary with links to your sources.',
     'Research online or ask the agency; don''t dig, bury or burn anything for this mission.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/bury-biomass), used with permission. Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'Biomass burial involves storing plant biomass, such as logs, woody debris, agricultural and forestry residues, and engineered bio-blocks, under conditions that prevent GHG-releasing decay – underground, above ground, or at ground level. Applications range from simple wood vaults buried underground to blocks of dried, compressed plant biomass sealed in impermeable barriers.',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/bury-biomass', null, null, null),
    ('7f666cb5-019d-5542-9809-9f8e606e13ab'::uuid, 'drawdown-use-methane-oxidizing-coatings',
     'A link or photo of your explainer with sources listed.',
     'Research and explain only; don''t experiment with gases or coatings.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/use-methane-oxidizing-coatings), used with permission. Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'Photocatalytic methane-oxidizing coatings applied to roofs and other surfaces exposed to air can convert methane molecules that contact the surface into CO₂.',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/use-methane-oxidizing-coatings', null, null, null),
